{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum","id":958806,"title":"Why is it so easy to root for the Circle against the Sanctum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-27T11:00:45-07:00","id":958806,"title":"Why is it so easy to root for the Circle against the Sanctum?","content":"Studying Cruac tends to Erode a vampires Humanity., studying Theban sorcery, forced him to grudgingly struggle to maintain his humanity<br /> <br /> The Circle Flouts societal conventions.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum generally upholds them<br /> <br /> why, given all of this, is it so easy to root for the Circle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:41:05-07:00","id":958818,"title":"","content":"Why would you root for either of them? They're not real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:50:04-07:00","id":958821,"title":"","content":"You've never rooted for the hero of a book or movie? Fictional has nothing to do with it. And a dismissive answer like that doesn't contribute to the thread.<br /> <br /> As for the OP, I can't claim to know for certain. However, given the content of the game, I can imagine it has to do with the oppressive Christian trappings of the Sanctum hitting home a bit more to many players. Vampire is the exact sort of game conservative Christian parents might tell a teen is satanic and forbidden. I mean, happened to me. Most people don't really grow up around pagans. Really, I think that's the root of it. We tend to root for the oppressed over the oppressors, and the meta-narrative both IC and OOC is that pagans are the ones that get oppressed, while the Christians do the oppressing. Not making blanket statements about either, but that's the typical narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:56:28-07:00","id":958824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958821#post958821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine it has to do with the oppressive Christian trappings of the Sanctum hitting home a bit more to many players.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, for me. I've long appreciated paganism over the more common religions. I was raised on stories of Greek, Roman, Norse and Egyptian mythology, after that I didn't really seize onto Abrahamic religions the way people seem to. Plus I've been literally chased by people calling me a 'bad' practitioner of religion by other members of that organized religion. Witches, on the other hand, have never tried to attack me.<br /> <br /> Plus I never got over my dislike of Solomon Birch, who was the main representative of the Lance in the fiction, which heavily influenced by opinions going into Vampire.<br /> <br /> Lastly, they're closer to my other favorite, Belial's Brood. Or at least they were in first edition.<br /> <br /> All that said, however, I do believe there's more fans of the Lancea et Sanctum here than the Circle of the Crone. I could be wrong, but a lot of people seem to like the Lance and dismiss the Circle as 'witches dancing around in the forest and being monsters.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-27-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:08:12-07:00","id":958828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958821#post958821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've never rooted for the hero of a book or movie? Fictional has nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, in actual narrative fiction. However, an RPG isn't generally narrative fiction, it's a book that describes a setting. I genuinely do find it very odd that people have that kind of attachment to groups in a fictional setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:33:18-07:00","id":958837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum#post958806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Studying Cruac tends to Erode a vampires Humanity., studying Theban sorcery, forced him to grudgingly struggle to maintain his humanity<br /> The Circle Flouts societal conventions.<br /> The Sanctum generally upholds them<br /> why, given all of this, is it so easy to root for the Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the answer is pretty simple - I'm not a fan of Christian frameworks anywhere.<br /> The Circle also feels more thematic for what I think of when I think of vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958828#post958828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, in actual narrative fiction. However, an RPG isn't generally narrative fiction, it's a book that describes a setting. I genuinely do find it very odd that people have that kind of attachment to groups in a fictional setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure TC is glad you felt the need to chime in for no other reason than to let them know that you find their attachments odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:45:57-07:00","id":958846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958824#post958824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, for me. I've long appreciated paganism over the more common religions. I was raised on stories of Greek, Roman, Norse and Egyptian mythology, after that I didn't really seize onto Abrahamic religions the way people seem to. Plus I've been literally chased by people calling me a 'bad' practitioner of religion by other members of that organized religion. Witches, on the other hand, have never tried to attack me.<br /> <br /> Plus I never got over my dislike of Solomon Birch, who was the main representative of the Lance in the fiction, which heavily influenced by opinions going into Vampire.<br /> <br /> Lastly, they're closer to my other favorite, Belial's Brood. Or at least they were in first edition.<br /> <br /> All that said, however, I do believe there's more fans of the Lancea et Sanctum here than the Circle of the Crone. I could be wrong, but a lot of people seem to like the Lance and dismiss the Circle as 'witches dancing around in the forest and being monsters.'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whats to dislike about Birch?<br /> <br /> Him breeding a family of slaves, his Advocating for the stupid &quot;Tranquility&quot; in chicago<br /> <br /> his refusal to even consider using pilfered knowledge of coils to improve his fellows unlives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:52:52-07:00","id":958851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958837#post958837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the answer is pretty simple - I'm not a fan of Christian frameworks anywhere. The Circle also feels more thematic for what I think of when I think of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I find odd. I mean, I agree it isn't terribly thematic in a traditional vampire sense, but the writers actually used it in a pretty original way. Just saying no, becuase you have some hangup with Christianity is really limiting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure TC is glad you felt the need to chime in for no other reason than to let them know that you find their attachments odd. </div> </div> </div>There is something to be said for having your views challenged. Frankly, I think it's a limiting way of viewing the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:05:50-07:00","id":958857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958846#post958846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats to dislike about Birch?<br /> <br /> Him breeding a family of slaves, his Advocating for the stupid &quot;Tranquility&quot; in chicago<br /> <br /> his refusal to even consider using pilfered knowledge of coils to improve his fellows unlives?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like his hobbies. I even appreciate his zeal, though obviously I don't share it. I think in terms of vampires, he's got the Requiem down and he's a great example of a powerful, though not elder-level vampire. But that's also why I don't like him. <i>He is a walking lie</i>.<br /> <br /> As much as I enjoy running them, I couldn't play a traditional vampire, I would find most of them unbearable to be around, for more reasons than worrying about them taking my blood or enslaving me. I tried to make my current werewolf more vampire-like in attitude but it fell flat. I'm just not made for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-27-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:12:26-07:00","id":958861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958851#post958851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something to be said for having your views challenged. Frankly, I think it's a limiting way of viewing the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're really interested, why not make a thread in the General Chronicles of Darkness board, so you can ask everyone who is a fan of one group over another, rather than only the Vampire players who would respond to this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:09:56-07:00","id":958885,"title":"","content":"The Sanctum follows more specific doctrines, doctrines that teach vampires to be dicks to humanity. With their philosophy of freedom and tolerance, acolytes can be much worse, but they aren't obliged so on the whole. This may differ in acolyte run cities, but fledglings are far more likely to get pushed around by the Sanctum, being part of the Western establishment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:24:28-07:00","id":958890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958818#post958818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you root for either of them? They're not real.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">As a reminder, rule 2 does include a proscription specifically against &quot;short messages or images which add nothing to a thread and serve only to express a user\u2019s displeasure with it.&quot; I don't think your intent here was to threadcrap, but in the future please try not to make posts like this.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:44:42-07:00","id":958892,"title":"","content":"My take on the matter: both Covenants are terrifying. They each represent the worst aspects and stereotypes of the religions they mimic, they both advocate discarding one's Humanity in favor of being a better Monster in service to their respective higher power(s), they both perform literal blood magic. To me, the CotC is more sympathetic (and I use the term relatively) for two main reasons: they're more honest about what they are (if the LeS are wolves in sheep's clothing, the CotC are just wolves), and their religious beliefs are more broad. I also agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> that a significant part of it is the fact that the audience VtR tends to appeal to (myself included) tends to have more baggage associated with Christianity than with Paganism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-27-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:48:33-07:00","id":958894,"title":"","content":"I would have said it's because the books always press the point that Lancea engage/engaged in literal genocide against the Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:50:20-07:00","id":958896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958894#post958894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have said it's because the books always press the point that Lancea engage/engaged in literal genocide against the Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda counted that as part of embodying the worst aspects of Christianity, given that the Inquisition was a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:51:05-07:00","id":958897,"title":"","content":"Neither covenant is &quot;good&quot; enough for me to root for; both preach horrific doctrines of inhuman monstrosity. As for why it's easier to side against the Sanctified, I think there's a bit of real-world bleedover in that plenty of people have had unpleasant experiences with Christian faiths, so having an evil vampire Catholic church is easy to hate. Comparatively few folks out there have been victimized by matriarchal evil pagan cults, and beyond that lots of the CofD fandom can either enjoy the exotic nature of such a thing or might actually be neopagans themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:01:55-07:00","id":958904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958821#post958821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, given the content of the game, I can imagine it has to do with the oppressive Christian trappings of the Sanctum hitting home a bit more to many players. Vampire is the exact sort of game conservative Christian parents might tell a teen is satanic and forbidden. I mean, happened to me. Most people don't really grow up around pagans. Really, I think that's the root of it. We tend to root for the oppressed over the oppressors, and the meta-narrative both IC and OOC is that pagans are the ones that get oppressed, while the Christians do the oppressing. Not making blanket statements about either, but that's the typical narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mania's hit the head of a pretty important nail, for me. The basic fact of the matter that the Sanctum orientates itself around being &quot;good Christian vampires&quot; is naturally going to alienate those who aren't interested in or actively reject a Christian view of the world.<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself, there's also the different perceptions fostered by the different lores underlying each Covenant's credo.<br /> <br /> The Circle's philosophy is that vampires are natural in their own right; being a vampire is a normal thing, nothing to be ashamed of - indeed, it's something to be proud of. Crones accept who they are and make peace with their nature, trying to live what they consider a &quot;good&quot; unlife without hypocritically denying that their nature requires them to prey upon and sometimes kill human beings. A vampire isn't really human anymore, and the Circle accepts that; but just because a wolf does not cry when it eats a bunny does not mean it can't try to be a responsible wolf.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum, on the other hand, seems to build itself around some of the worst perceivable aspects of Christianity; excessive self-flagellation (&quot;woe is me, for I am cursed by god and will never be shown his merciful light again&quot;), hypocritical self-righteousness (&quot;in my damnation, god has empowered me to act as his scourge upon the wicked&quot;) and aggressive proselytizing (&quot;all man must heed unto god, and my depredations will punish those who stray from the flock&quot;). It paints the Sanctified as, ironically, more monstrous than Crones; these are vampires who will justify all the evil they do as &quot;God's Work&quot;, adding the least appealing traits of a fanatic's mentality to the already unpleasant aspects of life as a vampire.<br /> <br /> This, to me at least, paints a mental portrait of the typical Sanctified as either a cringing, passive-aggressive beast with no pride in itself, or as a cruel, hypocritical fanatic, whilst the Crone's portrait is of a proud, self-assured and stable vampire who accepts what they are and owns it. I don't know about anyone else, but to me, this makes the Crones far more interesting and personally appealing.<br /> <br /> It's actually one of the reasons why I like Requiem far more than Masquerade. No explicitly canonical calcified Christian crap built into the very backbone of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:57:43-07:00","id":958960,"title":"","content":"Its just you? I find the Circle the most philosophically bankrupt of the three &quot;religion/philosophy&quot; covenants. The only thing it really has going for it is &quot;We'll teach you magic&quot; which seems to be why it collapses in the face of more proper faith based groups like the Shinto covenant in Tokyo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:43:13-07:00","id":958976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum#post958806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why, given all of this, is it so easy to root for the Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal bias, when you get right down to it. I personally don't have a preference for either over the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T18:28:30-07:00","id":959001,"title":"","content":"I have never really gotten the Lance in the same way I get the Circle. &quot;We're undead predators, let's not sugar coat our condition&quot; is just more appealing to me than &quot;We're God's chosen monsters, and we kill in his name&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:39:01-07:00","id":959055,"title":"","content":"There really is no way to answer the question beyond it is your personal bias. If you have a problem with Christianity then you have a bias against the Lance. People see what they want to see. This comes up with the Invictus and the Carthians too.<br /> <br /> Too many people miss the mark. Every covenant is morally bankrupt. Each one contains the worse kind of assholes you can imagine, in fact they are the ones in charge. Each covenant is meant to represent the worst stereotype of a certain belief system. The hope is that a player can see enough light in a covenant to thread the needle and not be forced to become the worst kind of asshole imaginable.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul are actually the ones that accept that they are no longer human and embrace being a vampire. What that means is up to the individual. The Circle have a specific definition for what it means to be a proper vampire, monster. In typical covenant hypocrisy, the covenant without rules has one of the most strict views on how a vampire should act.<br /> <br /> Having said that, there is nothing wrong with rooting for any of the covenants. Sometimes people root for the villain in a story even when they are written without any redeemable qualities. I think people at least recognize that they are rooting for the villain though. It is important to recognize what the covenants are and the role they play in society.<br /> <br /> There is a reason joining one is a breaking point. It isn't a good thing to do. Covenants are antagonists, even to a covenant's members. Covenants are bad, players don't have to be. They were all written to be equally bad so if you don't see the bad then you might want to look harder.<br /> <br /> The only thing that keeps the Circle from committing genocide is their lack of organization keeps them weak in most places. Generally, every covenant has a &quot;join or die&quot; attitude when they have the strength to pull it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T03:47:59-07:00","id":959164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=959055#post959055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really is no way to answer the question beyond it is your personal bias. If you have a problem with Christianity then you have a bias against the Lance. People see what they want to see. This comes up with the Invictus and the Carthians too.<br /> <br /> Too many people miss the mark. Every covenant is morally bankrupt. Each one contains the worse kind of assholes you can imagine, in fact they are the ones in charge. Each covenant is meant to represent the worst stereotype of a certain belief system. The hope is that a player can see enough light in a covenant to thread the needle and not be forced to become the worst kind of asshole imaginable.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul are actually the ones that accept that they are no longer human and embrace being a vampire. What that means is up to the individual. The Circle have a specific definition for what it means to be a proper vampire, monster. In typical covenant hypocrisy, the covenant without rules has one of the most strict views on how a vampire should act.<br /> <br /> Having said that, there is nothing wrong with rooting for any of the covenants. Sometimes people root for the villain in a story even when they are written without any redeemable qualities. I think people at least recognize that they are rooting for the villain though. It is important to recognize what the covenants are and the role they play in society.<br /> <br /> There is a reason joining one is a breaking point. It isn't a good thing to do. Covenants are antagonists, even to a covenant's members. Covenants are bad, players don't have to be. They were all written to be equally bad so if you don't see the bad then you might want to look harder.<br /> <br /> The only thing that keeps the Circle from committing genocide is their lack of organization keeps them weak in most places. Generally, every covenant has a &quot;join or die&quot; attitude when they have the strength to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought Belials brood was the very worst assholes...<br /> <br /> one other issue, anyone else study the real pagan religions because oif the Circle, and then start seriously exploring them IRL<br /> <br /> does that invalidate ones faith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T05:25:57-07:00","id":959182,"title":"","content":"Covenants provide a very important service to the vampire, they help hold back the beast by directing your Requiem towards &quot;Something&quot;. Invictus power and feudalism, Carthians social justice, Ordo transcendence, the Lance and its faith.<br /> <br /> the Circle provides nothing, it says its ok to give into the beast. It says its ok to lose yourself. its actively detrimental to the long term development of a Kindred. The Ume and Kigan are more honest about the whole damned thing and provide a framework that's not a short trip down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T10:16:07-07:00","id":959320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=959182#post959182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Circle provides nothing, it says its ok to give into the beast. It says its ok to lose yourself. its actively detrimental to the long term development of a Kindred. The Ume and Kigan are more honest about the whole damned thing and provide a framework that's not a short trip down.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle offer understanding about the nature of the Beast and Humanity.<br /> <br /> It is not about how low can you go. It's about appreciating what every bit of Humanity you've shed meant, what you are becoming, and embracing it.<br /> <br /> Losing all your Humanity isn't even part of their goal. The goal is being someone who can live with themselves without lying to themselves about what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-28-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T12:53:55-07:00","id":959971,"title":"","content":"I think I prefer the Lance over the Crone as the Lance has a single body you can be intelligently addressed.*<br /> <br /> Every coven does its own thing, with only its blood magic as testament to the power of its faith.<br /> <br /> The Lance has scholars and creeds. I could get behind it even if it didn't have Theban.<br /> <br /> It is all well and good to say 'You're natural. Embrace it.' It is quite another to back that claim up with something I can chew on.<br /> <br /> I think the Circle is the only Covenant some variant of myself couldn't join. I can see an Invictus me, a Carthian me, a Dragon me, and even a Sanctified me but no Acolyte me.<br /> <br /> *I could be wrong on this but it is the impression I have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:12:34-07:00","id":960143,"title":"","content":"I prefer lancea. Christian-themed vampires always remind me of castlevania, so bonus points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T00:01:17-07:00","id":960272,"title":"","content":"I like both of them and try not to play favorites.In their own way they are interesting and adds to the setting, even if I personally like damnation as a theme for vampires rather than empowerment. But I like the theme to be dark. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T00:59:25-07:00","id":960288,"title":"","content":"As an athiest with no love for religion of any kind, I totally dig the Sanctified, and as much as I want to appreciate the Crones... and they do have some cool things... they just fall flat for me overall.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason I like the Caine mythology of VtM. Of course it's all crap, but as a work of fiction, Christianity is just more compelling to me than paganism, and fits the vampire theme of damnation so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:50:17-07:00","id":960319,"title":"","content":"From my standpoint the LS is just a better written an interesting covenant with a working and understandable social structure and philosophy/theology. The CoC is just flat and unusable beyond neopagan-stereotypes and without a functional place in society or even a feasable social structure and their philosophy and 'theology' is just sadly just flat nomatter how much time the ST tries to bind the local religion/paganism into it, it allways fall flat. This as well as that the CoC-book is one of the worst books to VtR in my oppinion, its just a shitload apologies about how no cult is like another... Shit we get that, neither are the other covenants in different cities but we need some common ground to work from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:30:45-07:00","id":960342,"title":"","content":"I think that more people root for the Circle because of a few biases. Not only because of the RL Christianity angle (though I personally find that the LeS has several key redemptive features that make them my favorite covenant philosphically), but also because of the clear favoritism of Cruac over Theban.<br /> <br /> To put it bluntly? Cruac gets all the best rituals. In 1e, Cruac ended up with roughly <i>double the amount of rituals</i>. From the beginning, Cruac's gotten more random rituals in books than Theban. Sure, the covenant and core books had the same amount of rituals, but Cruac got more from random appearances like in Gangrel clan book, more Cruac rituals than Theban in Cotires, etc. And, even in the case of those rituals, most of the Cruac ones were considered by many to be more useful than many Theban ones. Especially the divination rituals. Theban generally ended up being used for combat magic in my experience, and little else.<br /> <br /> And don't get me started on the sacrifices. Some sacrifices are so heavy that makes the effect of the ritual not worthwhile, or exceedingly narrow in application. Others are simply difficult to arrange. One player complained to me that the sacrifices made him feel like he was a D&amp;D wizard carrying around a spell component pouch. And the difficulty of the sacrifices stacks on top the usual willpower expendature. Meanwhile, Cruac is a point of vitae, and done (the new mantles need willpower as well, but I think that's more of an exception than rule).<br /> <br /> And then, there's the themes of the magic themselves. Cruac, despite the CotC's pretence at vampire-neo-paganism, tends to have rituals that tend towards powers that vampires classically have in fiction. Vampiric gardens, storm raising, dark divinations, gargoyles and homoculi and other horrors, etc. Meanwhile, Theban is pretty much just &quot;Abrahamic + ancient Egypt&quot; themed magic. While cool in its own right, Theban tends to support more narrow character concepts/flavors than Cruac. At least, that's my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T05:14:27-07:00","id":960367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960342#post960342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Cruac ended up with roughly <i>double the amount of rituals</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very roughly, it seems. Cruac has 58 to Theban's 51.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:15:48-07:00","id":960416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960367#post960367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very roughly, it seems. Cruac has 58 to Theban's 51.</div> </div> </div> </div>Count again. Cruac surpasses the total number of Theban Sorcery rituals by level 3. And that isn't counting Spirit Cruac, Sethite Cruac, Veneficia, Lithopedia or the fact that in 2nd edition Theban Sorcery rituals can be converted to Cruac now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:17:06-07:00","id":960417,"title":"","content":"Cruac also tends to be cast as the persecuted covenant, with the Lance trying to purge the heathans. Cruac is rarely on the offense in the fiction, on a broad level. On a personal level, sure, they are monsters. On the *institutional* level they are almost always the undersogs or the victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T08:26:02-07:00","id":960452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960416#post960416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Count again. Cruac surpasses the total number of Theban Sorcery rituals by level 3. And that isn't counting Spirit Cruac, Sethite Cruac, Veneficia, Lithopedia or the fact that in 2nd edition Theban Sorcery rituals can be converted to Cruac now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was counting Sethite Cruac, but I wasn't counting Lithopedia because it's not Cruac, it's bloodline magic from the Ordo Dracul. Veneficia <i>is</i> Cruac, but considered extinct and existed mostly as copies of modern Cruac abilities, though if you do count it only adds 7 to the number.<br /> <br /> Where are you getting your numbers from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T08:36:01-07:00","id":960459,"title":"","content":"Sure, if you count activities like snatching newborn babies out of a hospital for a human sacrificial rite to enhance an act of cannibalism, hunting and killing humans for sport, and ritualistically murdering servants because their god tells them to do it, as the activities of innocent victims, then yeah, I guess Acolytes qualify.<br /> <br /> <br /> ADD ON<br /> <br /> The whitewolf.wikia has the Cruac and Theban rituals. Cruac has 79, Theban has 55. Again, it's not taking into account Lithopedia (which requires Cruac proficiency to use) or Veneficia (which is described as Cruac but with slightly different mechanics) <br /> I'm not counting how a Cruac user with Spirit Cruac can effectively replicate numerous Mage spells or Werewolf rituals in that total but I do concur with MCN's statement that Cruac gets the spells that let them do pretty much everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-30-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:11:01-07:00","id":960481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960416#post960416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the fact that in 2nd edition Theban Sorcery rituals can be converted to Cruac now.</div> </div> </div> </div> Didn't that Reclamation merit get pulled? Or are you talking about something else? <br /> <br /> But, yeah, I included all the Settite, Venefica, bloodline powers, etc when counting Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:39:58-07:00","id":960502,"title":"","content":"I've no idea if it got pulled but yes Glorious Reclamation was the merit I was referring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:47:53-07:00","id":960506,"title":"","content":"In 1e my favourite covenant was was the Ordo Dracol followed by the Circle of the Crone. The Ordo won out due to being more accommodating of my hopes of avoiding Humanity loss with no frenzy and go nights on one blood edging out immune to stakes and blood bonds even though I really liked the Circles &quot;we don't have all the answers and don't claim we do&quot; outlook in the core book. Come 2e Ordo are still my favourite with being able to spend the day active appealing to my pro Humanity leanings and hyper enslaving blood appealing to my desire to amass power and control but the Circle just aren't as appealing as they were with the fluff no longer emphasising the stuff I picked up on last edition.<br /> To sum up I agree that the Circle has cooler powers than the Lance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:54:19-07:00","id":960545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960459#post960459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, if you count activities like snatching newborn babies out of a hospital for a human sacrificial rite to enhance an act of cannibalism, hunting and killing humans for sport, and ritualistically murdering servants because their god tells them to do it, as the activities of innocent victims, then yeah, I guess Acolytes qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at you specifically, but when I said in my earlier post that the Crones have some cool things, this is the kind of thing that makes me want to like them more than I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:44:41-07:00","id":960715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960459#post960459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, if you count activities like snatching newborn babies out of a hospital for a human sacrificial rite to enhance an act of cannibalism, hunting and killing humans for sport, and ritualistically murdering servants because their god tells them to do it, as the activities of innocent victims, then yeah, I guess Acolytes qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing victim is pretty easy, even for mass-murdering dirt-bags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:56:31-07:00","id":960724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960502#post960502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've no idea if it got pulled but yes Glorious Reclamation was the merit I was referring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wheres this Merit found if I could ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:41:33-07:00","id":960810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960724#post960724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wheres this Merit found if I could ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere. It <i>used to be</i> in the &quot;Acolyte Merits and Rituals&quot; playtest document for Secrets of the Covenants, but it was removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:14:29-07:00","id":960821,"title":"","content":"In regards to the OP, It's easy to root for the Circle because they are best covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:24:59-07:00","id":960826,"title":"","content":"It was removed because of Balance considerations? or because it was seen as saying potentialy undesirable things about theban sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:29:54-07:00","id":960829,"title":"","content":"I've heard it said that we dislike our heretics more than we dislike our pagans. Regardless of the truth of the statement, I feel it sums up my relationship with the Circle and Lance. From an aesthetic level, the Lance is way more interesting; at the same time, however, their theology is utterly repugnant. Ironically, I'd be more likely to make a Sanctified character (even if they'd probably be more of a &quot;What have I gotten involved with and how can I get out?&quot; Type) because, honestly, I don't hate the Circle, but I'm just not fond of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:31:05-07:00","id":960830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960826#post960826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was removed because of Balance considerations? or because it was seen as saying potentialy undesirable things about theban sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:56:57-07:00","id":960839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960826#post960826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was removed because of Balance considerations? or because it was seen as saying potentialy undesirable things about theban sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it was officially responded to, but the point was brought up that with <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Blood_Sorcery:_Sacraments_%26_Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Sorcery</a>, a practitioner of either art has effective access to the rituals of the other already. This would, obviously, make such a Merit redundant and a waste of Experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:59:46-07:00","id":961027,"title":"","content":"oh a problem with blood sorcery I have is how do I construct the rituals found in Nomad's or Coteries<br /> <br /> or the sanctum or Crone books.<br /> <br /> The Harai ritual of the Amanotsukai breaks quite a few rules on Cruac.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:25:55-07:00","id":961125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=961027#post961027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Harai ritual of the Amanotsukai breaks quite a few rules on Cruac.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it would make more sense for them to develop a mystery, albeit a mystery with more emphasis on scales than coils, rather than something like Cruac or Kigan. Although they may have origins amongst Kigan sorcerers, having decided to stop wallowing in corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:56:03-07:00","id":961183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960826#post960826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was removed because of Balance considerations? or because it was seen as saying potentialy undesirable things about theban sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because of thematic concerns. When the merit was first released, it was highly controversial because (in the eyes of many people) it effectively turned Theban into a watered down version of Cruac instead of something within its own right. In general, there seems to be a desire to have Theban and Cruac have distinct power sets and abilities with little overlap, each standing on its own abilities. This merit kind of threatened to undermine that difference, as well as remove the potential for Livian heretics and other cross-covenant shinanigans.<br /> <br /> At least, that was my take away from reading the comments and thread when it came to complaints. You can see all of those still if you check out the Acolyte blog for that particular release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:20:36-07:00","id":961201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum#post958806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Circle Flouts societal conventions...<br /> <br /> why, given all of this, is it so easy to root for the Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Culture induced bias towards the ideolization of the 'rebel' and 'maverick' archetypes, the 'bad boys who play by thier own rules' even though in real life such people are dangerous selfish antisocial personalities who'd likely be stripped of thier status (the Lethal Weapon's character Riggs is a perfect example) due to instability and legitimate safety concerns.<br /> <br /> That is my rational analysis because I no longer share that near universal emotional urging to root for &quot;underdogs/rebels/mavericks&quot; unless the status quo is truly tyrannical or thoroughly corrupt, as I did when I was a younger man or as a boy. As I've aged specific context seems more important than broad stereotypes. Reality just seem too complex for easy answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-31-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T15:47:50-07:00","id":961271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=961201#post961201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Culture induced bias towards the ideolization of the 'rebel' and 'maverick' archetypes, the 'bad boys who play by thier own rules' even though in real life such people are dangerous selfish antisocial personalities who'd likely be stripped of thier status (the Lethal Weapon's character Riggs is a perfect example) due to instability and legitimate safety concerns.<br /> <br /> That is my rational analysis because I no longer share that near universal emotional urging to root for &quot;underdogs/rebels/mavericks&quot; unless the status quo is truly tyrannical or thoroughly corrupt, as I did when I was a younger man or as a boy. As I've aged specific context seems more important than broad stereotypes. Reality just seem too complex for easy answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think this 'bias' causes more people to like the Carthians, in favor of the Invictus? While the Circle are focused on the self, the Carthians fit the rebel 'bad boys who play by their own rules' stereotype far more. They even have their own system of rules to play by and make sure you let them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-31-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T16:49:16-07:00","id":961285,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I'd say I &quot;root for&quot; either the Lance or the Circle over the other, as none of the Covenants really hold any sort of moral or ideological high ground, but I do generally find the Lance more interesting. It's an entirely personal bias, but I've never been able to take neopaganism seriously as anything other than self-aware contrarian artifice. Even the Circle's naturalist predator philosophy is rooted more in nineteenth century reactions to modernity than in anything terribly ancient. They say that they abjure any kind of organized theology right before saying that they are made up of a cluster of wildly differing cults, which doesn't make much sense to me as each of these cults presumably contains its own organized theology. They may not impose that specific theology over the entire Covenant but one has to imagine they cleave to it pretty jealously within their own temples, otherwise it isn't much of a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:39:00-07:00","id":961305,"title":"","content":"Huh. I asked myself what are my favorite covenants and I noticed a pattern. I wonder what it tells about me as a person.<br /> [from least to the most favorite]<br /> Crone --&gt; Carthian--&gt;Lancea--&gt;Invictus--&gt;Ordo Dracul<br /> Seems I don't like the &quot;chaotic&quot; alignment, so to speak! Though Crone is special, as it's the only Covenant I didn't create a single character concept for ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:08:34-07:00","id":961314,"title":"","content":"I'd say rooting for the CotC is easier because:<br /> 1)People like rooting for the perceived underdog<br /> 2)Witches are cooler than preachers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:19:07-07:00","id":961863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=959971#post959971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every coven does its own thing, with only its blood magic as testament to the power of its faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the actual answer to the OP's question. The Acolytes vary enough to be more things to more people, and rooting for your favourite idea for a coven easily turns into rooting for the covenant as a whole.<br /> <br /> (In the 1st edition sourcebook, we even see Christian-themed Acolytes, and humane ones who eschew Cruac).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:37:50-07:00","id":961874,"title":"","content":"I think it's got a lot to do with fluff and aesthetics (a reader prefers how one covenant is described and depicted over the other), the goals that characters of either covenant can have (the Acolyte's &quot;I'm a vampire who has no hangups about it&quot; vs. the Sanctified's &quot;I'm tempting and punishing mortals for the Lord&quot;), and the powers that you get for joining either one (Cr\u00faac vs. Theban Sorcery). Playing a vampire who doesn't mind being one, even enjoys it, is easy to do if you're an Acolyte; playing a femme fatale/homme fatale seductress/seducer or vigilante is easy to do if you're a Sanctified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:49:53-07:00","id":963199,"title":"","content":"From what I've seen with the various players I've had, it's not as clear cut. I live in Europe, nutty religious upbringing and roleplayer witch hunts aren't as common as they seem to be in the US from what I read sometimes. Gamers can easily be percived as immature manchildren, but nobody would actually go on tv and seriously call them satanists. I dunno, maybe they do that in Norway or Finland, but I haven't seen or lived that here. That doesn't mean the Lancea is seen as a great thing, but it's nothing personal usually. Lots of people I game with are atheists and don't see a church like group as an enviable form of government. We also probably easily liken it to Catholic Chuch which, depending on your point of view and/or what historical period you're talking about, can be a pretty decadent, tyrannical and corrupt body with a lot of political power, so while the crazy zealot bunch is part of the Lancea imagery, it's also easy to see it as a kind of more spiritual Invictus.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen, people seem to consider the Carthians the default &quot;good guys&quot; and the Ordo, a nice option. I've had one player I threw into the Lancea Sanctum's arms and who made his next character part of it when that one died, another one who wanted to play in it from the get go. One character joined the Circle after I revealed his sire was the head acolyte in town and another one could have joined, but then got tired of her character and made a new one. So when it comes to my players, they seem to prefer playing Lancea than Circle, but that may be also because of how I play them.<br /> <br /> As a GM, I actually tend to prefer using the Lance et Sanctum. It allows me to easily defy player expectations. To me, the decadent, tyrannical and corrupt thing is pretty cool (like it is for the Invictus) because it doesn't mean the covenant is necessarily evil or good, but that it's a mess of potential internal conspiracy to be the one who's seen as the cool priest. I don't like to make them villains or good guys, just very ambiguous and let players decide if they're willing to side with them occasionally. One of the biggest dignitaries of the Lancea, the Cardinal (or former Cardinal) of Rome is actually a pretty decent guy. Shady and perfectly willing to order a hit on someone if he thinks it's necessary, but usually fair and willing to help when it can improve the image of the convenant. Sometimes, it's just funny to let players be paranoid towards a religious figure they would instinctively distrust only to shock them with the fact he's not that bad.<br /> <br /> I also tend to have trouble portraying the Circle of the Crone for a variety of reasons. For one, while I can easily picture (even if it's inaccurate in the end) a corrupt church, a corrupt aristocracy, a shady mad scientist/freemason cell or whatever the carthians can appear as, the pretty alien nature of how the circle of the crone seems to function is hard for me to translate in game. Usually, I kind of protray them as a ragtag bunch of various pagan cults or one local variant of that. It's still kind of shallow so I usually try to throw some flavor at the players and hope they don't dig too far. I just usually don't really see how that thing would work while not looking too much like the other covenants. Reading the covenant book actually helped a bunch. I really liked the whole mythological roles thing with the maiden, hero, lady in red, etc. I thought that was great stuff and I find it's a good basis for creating NPCs.<br /> <br /> The other reason is their whole being monsters thing, and the covenant book didn't really help with that. I mean, wow, if a city group of, like, 15 to 20 acolytes did half the stuff described in the book, their humanity would plummet like crazy. They're barely better than Belial's brood. Maybe it's just me and I usually do softcore vampire in terms of how cruel and dismissive towards killing my NPCs are, but still, There's just something borderline caricatural in the way the Circle is depicted sometimes. From the book : &quot;If all were perfect, they could build a grand sanctuary in the middle of the city, as dark and magnificent as the gods themselves. The light of the moon would shine upon pillars of black marble laced with fire-red carnelian.&quot; I mean, wow, I didn't know losing your humanity also meant losing your sense of good taste.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, I guess whatever the covenant, I always take a step back from the official books so I can portray them as actually working. Plus, I dunno, but me and my players can only take so much stumbling upon baby being sacrified by a mustache twirling witch. I like to make my NPCs act for actual reasons and not be unnecessarily cruel (even a vampire that's mostly surrendered to the beast, to me, will be violent because someone is in the way, not going out of their way to murder kids for kicks), and I guess that makes them not that monstrous (the other side is the actually raving and more &quot;evil&quot; NPCs stand out more). From experience, I'd say that fits me and my players just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:40:26-07:00","id":963559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=961271#post961271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think this 'bias' causes more people to like the Carthians, in favor of the Invictus? While the Circle are focused on the self, the Carthians fit the rebel 'bad boys who play by their own rules' stereotype far more. They even have their own system of rules to play by and make sure you let them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I understand what you are saying, but Carthians are an alternative political system to the Invictus, not a broad catch-all label for those radically varying from western materialism/secular politics (Carthians) or the divine right authority/feudalism (Invictus) as the Circle is. Governments, monothistic faiths, and any politics are by thier nature institutions that imply playing by rules and are the establishment against which to rebel. Ordo and Circle are the &quot;scientific&quot; and spiritual free agents of the Danse Macabre, the Ordo doing research and the Circle as a grab bag of ancient faiths, neither necessarily politically uniform even within a single Domain. Yes there is variation among Carthians but they are not the Anarch Movement of Classic World of Darkness, and can easily be as totaltarian as the Invictus's reputation.<br /> <br /> Also politics of the last couple decades are seriously disenchanting the notion that some how there is any political system which isn't predacated on corruption and abuse of authority. I've seen billboards saying &quot;This country cannot survive another 8 years of Hope and Change.&quot; which is a strong statement given how powerful those ideals resonate in the aspirations of many, and I believe transcends specific party dissatisfaction to be general political dissatisfaction. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-05-2016, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T03:07:35-07:00","id":963614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=961314#post961314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> 2)Witches are cooler than preachers</div> </div> </div> </div> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=421\" data-tempid=\"temp_421_1473070007965_455\" /><br /> <br /> Nah, preachers are way cooler than witches. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:13:50-07:00","id":963802,"title":"","content":"I must say that this is a very interesting thread.<br /> <br /> And I entirely support the notion that the Carthians can be as, or more, authoritarian than the Invictus. Maybe I should dig up my old &quot;Carthians in power&quot; thread and bring it back to the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:21:58-07:00","id":964103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum#post958806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Studying Cruac tends to Erode a vampires Humanity., studying Theban sorcery, forced him to grudgingly struggle to maintain his humanity<br /> <br /> The Circle Flouts societal conventions.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum generally upholds them<br /> <br /> why, given all of this, is it so easy to root for the Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well for one thing, the Sanctum believe that it is their purpose to take up <b>Satan's</b> role of testing the faithful... I think when you look at the devil and say <i>&quot;this is part of His plan&quot;</i> your organization comes off as a bunch of crazy ass holes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Few things are more terrifying than a fanatic. Except maybe a fanatic with immortality and access to biblical curses!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the Circle has more freedom of religion and philosophy.<br /> <br /> Paganism in and of itself is not a religion. Paganism is typically defined as a religion that doesn't adhere to the Abrahamic faiths (Christianity, Hebrew, Islam). So when you use the word Pagan, you could be referring to one of any number of different religious groups and practices. <br /> <br /> If you want to, you can play a Gangrel warrior who believes an honorable death will earn him a place in Valhalla. Thus casting the CotC in a more favorably light than the simple <i>&quot;Meh, blood magic!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-06-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:02:06-07:00","id":964123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=959182#post959182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Covenants provide a very important service to the vampire, they help hold back the beast by directing your Requiem towards &quot;Something&quot;. Invictus power and feudalism, Carthians social justice, Ordo transcendence, the Lance and its faith.<br /> <br /> the Circle provides nothing, it says its ok to give into the beast. It says its ok to lose yourself. its actively detrimental to the long term development of a Kindred. The Ume and Kigan are more honest about the whole damned thing and provide a framework that's not a short trip down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think you're confusing acceptance with indulgence.<br /> <br /> Somebody earlier pointed out how a wolf doesn't cry for killing a rabbit, and that's a pretty good example.<br /> <br /> Predators kill to survive. That is an indisputable fact of life. But that doesn't mean the predator is running around slaughtering its prey on sight. It takes what it needs to survive without endangering its environment. The exception for this comes as a result of over population when there isn't enough food to go around.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a member of the Circle, you are taught that it's okay to feed on humans. It's part of what you are, now. But that doesn't mean it's okay to run through the streets tearing people to shreds! Have some self control, man!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Lancea gives you the thumbs up to reenact the Story of Job on an innocent man (fuck his life completely), just to see if he still worships God or not!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-06-2016, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T12:23:01-07:00","id":964465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964123#post964123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predators kill to survive. That is an indisputable fact of life. But that doesn't mean the predator is running around slaughtering its prey on sight. It takes what it needs to survive without endangering its environment. The exception for this comes as a result of over population when there isn't enough food to go around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, predators can often be mass murderers. What usually saves the prey is that taking one out gives enough time for the rest of the group to run or circle up. When the prey is confined (fox in the hen house) or too stupid/defenseless to get away, the predator will just slaughter all of them. It makes conservationists' jobs hard. If lions only took one cow at a time, herdsmen could write it off as cost of doing business. But when they slaughter dozens, it's tough to tell people they shouldn't be shot on sight.<br /> <br /> But looking through that lens I think paints your real point brighter - the Sanctified aren't stupid, uncontrolled predators. They are predators with a purpose, and the self-control to see God's will writ on the world. Acting like mindless beasts (like the Circle) moves away from that will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:09:54-07:00","id":964555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964465#post964465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, predators can often be mass murderers. What usually saves the prey is that taking one out gives enough time for the rest of the group to run or circle up. When the prey is confined (fox in the hen house) or too stupid/defenseless to get away, the predator will just slaughter all of them. It makes conservationists' jobs hard. If lions only took one cow at a time, herdsmen could write it off as cost of doing business. But when they slaughter dozens, it's tough to tell people they shouldn't be shot on sight.<br /> <br /> But looking through that lens I think paints your real point brighter - the Sanctified aren't stupid, uncontrolled predators. They are predators with a purpose, and the self-control to see God's will writ on the world. Acting like mindless beasts (like the Circle) moves away from that will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except that the Circle also seem to act with an intelligence. Like I said, they aren't running down the city street massacring people. They accept that they're vampires, but they don't make a grand show about it. And I don't know about you, but if I get killed by a vampire, I'd prefer to think the vampire is just doing what it needs to survive, instead of being told &quot;God wants to punish me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> What you're accusing them of is more in theme with Belial's Brood, who actually want to devolve into Draugr, because they think a vampire is supposed to have zero humanity left.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood are demon worshipers; they believe that vampires are supposed to be mindless beasts who lust for destruction and mayhem. Which is far more extreme than simply taking what you need and leaving the rest alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:02:25-07:00","id":964684,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the multi-post, but going to add this bit of idea in here.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum is primarily about <b>self loathing</b>. They make it very clear to you that you are damned and nothing you do will ever cleanse you of your sins. You're going to hell regardless of what you do. But before you get there, you might as well make sure you earn that damnation by terrorizing human society. That, to me, sounds like they're just looking for an excuse to harass people. Which makes them giant, blood sucking ass holes, in my book!<br /> <br /> <br /> By contrast, the Circle of the Crone is primarily about <b>self respect</b>. Your condition may be tragic, but it is manageable. You can be a monster without being <i>a monster</i> about it. And unlike the Abrahamic faiths, the Circle has a variety of gods and goddesses who would be willing to accept them, instead of condemning them for circumstances beyond their control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-06-2016, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T00:50:08-07:00","id":964835,"title":"","content":"As the Circle of the Crone is currently written, Belial's Brood would be a faction within the Circle unless they opted out for some reason. That is my point about covenants. The Circle would willingly accept Belial's Brood and fight to defend them against the other covenants. The other covenants would accept factions just as bad as the Brood. To think that any are good or something to root for must be the result of some sort of bias. Covenants are bad, even though individual members are not.<br /> <br /> I don't see self respect as what the Circle is about, but I guess that it is one interpretation. They oppose every other covenant's beliefs and are spiritual if we are to be literal and precise. They don't seem to consider being a vampire a curse at all. Whatever downsides some others might consider would be viewed as inherent qualities of existence. People need to breathe. People don't consider that a weakness or a curse. It is just the way things are.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess all the fanboying of a particular covenant does at least give insight into a character's perspective. Personally, if it was my choice, I would pick the group with the best toys and get out to go independent as soon as I could. They all seem like scary assholes to me. This was the intention. It's a horror game, not a dark superhero game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:33:53-07:00","id":964853,"title":"","content":"I think there are countless ways to view any covenant and interpret their credo (and that's what I like about them, you could justify both being a very nice person and a complete psycho with the right arguments). In its worst light, the Lancea et Sanctum is a bunch of fanatics who build their existence around the goal of finding the purest persons and messing with their lives to see how long it takes them to snap. They're nihilistic jaded assholes who don't have anything to lose anymore and will do anything to live up to their beliefs and ensure other vampires do the same or die.<br /> <br /> But logically, that description should only concern a minority of the covenant. That stuff is a lot to accept and it's not realaly anything to look forward to. A few extremely violent people will dive into it and use it as a means to act without moral restrains and be admired for it. Still, I'd think that kind of person is rare. Unless they're very intelligent, they would attract attention sooner or later. The Lancea forbids killing other vampires and that might be a means to ensure that these people don't trigger open wars with other covenants, but such extreme individuals aren't constrained by rules very long. If they need to, they'll find a loophole, make excuses that it doesn't really count in a variety of cases (the Catholic Church didn't have any problems with &quot;thou shlat not kill&quot; when they called for the crusades). Point is, a covenant composed of too many of those people would make for a very unstable political scene and they probably wouldn't live long for most of them.<br /> <br /> The more positive aspect of the Lancea is that it gives the same thing other covenants do. You may say it's about self loathing and resigning to damnation, but that's not entirely true. From what I think I remember, the Lancea doesn't rule out hope of redemption, but that's a distant hope and only if you fulfil your role. The Lancea Sanctum, even more than other covenants, is about acceptance of one's fate. You are damned, you survive by preying on other living beings and the sun kills you. There is no way out of there, but that doesn't mean you have to lose hope. Even in this condition you have a place in the world. You are needed. You can go crazy and become a beast, but you can do and be better than that.<br /> <br /> The Invictus teaches you that being undead doesn't mean you have to give up your dreams and ambition. You can still accumulate power behind the scenes or get behind someone who has that power and is ready to give a small portion to you. The Carthian movement teaches you that the vampire society is unjust and that you can do something and fight the elders' power. The Ordo Dracul teaches you that you don't have to be content being what you have become. You can be more if you're willing to put in the hard work, and the sky's the limit. The Circle of the Crone, I assume, teaches you that it's okay to be a vampire. Monsters are just another type of being. What happened to you didn't put you outside the world and you're definitely not alone. Just accept what you are and do what comes natural. The Lancea Sanctum teaches you that all those teachings get old after a while. Power can only last so long and you'll get bored eventually and make a mistake. Fighting elders and the Man is a vain and endless struggle. One day, you'll get careless and die or you'll become the elder and then what ? The quest to better oneself is an illusion. Some things are better left alone and you don't need to be better, you already are exactly what you are supposed to be. Finally, yes you are a monster, but you are not just a normal part of the world anymore. The beast will eventually betray you and nothing will hold you back from becoming an abomination.<br /> <br /> The Lancea gives lots and desperate vampires a goal, something immaterial to look forward to. It gives them a faith to cling to when their requiem gets tough. When you doubt, you can turn to a priest or bishop who will honestly listen to you. They won't demand loyalty like the prince or give you a bomb and tell you to blow up the elyseum like the firebrand. Sure, the principles are kinda violent, but you're there for a reason, you're making a difference and you're working for the greater good. You're doing what needs to be done, what nobody else can or should do.<br /> <br /> That's the vibe I get if I try to paint them in a positive light. I'm thinking most Lancea members aren't very active in their activity of trolling mortals. That's actually kind of hard and a lot of work. I'd imagine most of those who try either select one person and see where they can go with them (within the limit of how far they are personnally ready to go) or go from mortal to mortal, doing bad things to them like once or twice before moving on. A good number of sanctified, mostly recent members would probably want to hold off for a while, pay lip service to the faith, but not really doing much and just being happy with having church buddies they can talk to when they get lonely. A lot of time would also probably be spent discussing the faith, the texts, doing mass, confessions, and stuff. Finally, there's politicking. A cult has power dynamics. Status, recognition (inside and outside the covenant) attract most people. The Invictus is associated with power and money, but powerful priests and bishops have power over other sanctified. They can get money easily and have a pretty good life. And it's not necessarily a bad thing for other convenants. A bishop who values their expensive cars, luxurious apartments and private receptions will think twice before making too much wave or going to war against a rival covenant. These are vampires who may be bargained with. Some of them may also see the Lancea for what is is good for, not only a holy mission and/or a private army, but also a home for younger vampires, a way to make them feel better about the whole deal and stop them from rampaging left and right out of spite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:13:18-07:00","id":964888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964853#post964853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If they need to, they'll find a loophole, make excuses that it doesn't really count in a variety of cases (the Catholic Church didn't have any problems with &quot;thou shlat not kill&quot; when they called for the crusades).</div> </div> </div> </div> Nitpick - its actually &quot;thou shall not murder,&quot; which is a much different definition. From the earliest texts, self defense and military action have never been covered by the commandment. I mean, hells. The hebrews immediately went to war to take Isreal immediately after getting the tablets! That's not a loophole, its a modern interpretation of an ancient text. <br /> <br /> Some people are fond of saying that words mean things. What those people don't mention is that words mean different things to different people, and that what words mean changes over time and location.<br /> <br /> Now, lets apply this to talking about the Sanctified's relationship to their commandments, the Three Traditions. Masquerade, Progeny and Diablarie. From the very beginning, the LeS aren't outright forbidding any of those... well, at least the first two, I can't remember details of the third. Ghouling and feeding are innately Masquerade breaches. Scaring mortals onto the straight and narrow is a Masquerade breach. A vampire's very life is filled with breaches of the Masquerade. Childer are also another inevitability. The Curse wants to spread. Vampires come with reproductive urges to make more like themselves. This is also another LeS understanding. <br /> <br /> Vampires don't have strict laws. Their covenant wouldn't survive with it - exceptions must exist by the vampire's very nature. So, the LeS have guidelines instead of a code. That makes things far more fluid without the need of excuses or loopholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:09:36-07:00","id":965026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964835#post964835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Circle of the Crone is currently written, Belial's Brood would be a faction within the Circle unless they opted out for some reason. That is my point about covenants. The Circle would willingly accept Belial's Brood and fight to defend them against the other covenants. The other covenants would accept factions just as bad as the Brood. To think that any are good or something to root for must be the result of some sort of bias. Covenants are bad, even though individual members are not.<br /> <br /> I don't see self respect as what the Circle is about, but I guess that it is one interpretation. They oppose every other covenant's beliefs and are spiritual if we are to be literal and precise. They don't seem to consider being a vampire a curse at all. Whatever downsides some others might consider would be viewed as inherent qualities of existence. People need to breathe. People don't consider that a weakness or a curse. It is just the way things are.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess all the fanboying of a particular covenant does at least give insight into a character's perspective. Personally, if it was my choice, I would pick the group with the best toys and get out to go independent as soon as I could. They all seem like scary assholes to me. This was the intention. It's a horror game, not a dark superhero game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Except as explained earlier, Paganism is not a unified religion. It's a word used to describe non-Abrahamic faiths. You can not slap a generic summary onto the Circle of the Crone's belief system, unlike the Lancea Sanctum who are an organized religion. Each cult functions differently and may have different beliefs compared to others within the same faction. I see what you're saying about how the Brood could be considered a branch of the Crone. <i>But you must remember that not every cult is going to feel the same way.</i><br /> <br /> First edition core book of Requiem goes onto explain that some members of the Circle try to balance out the negative actions with creative hobbies, such as painting or gardening. So clearly they're not just a bunch of blood mages looking to strut their stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> And besides, the very same argument could be applied to the Lancea as well. They preach that it is their purpose to fulfill Satan's roll on earth. What better way to do that than to sign on with Belial's Brood, who believe that vampires are supposed to act like demons?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964888#post964888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, lets apply this to talking about the Sanctified's relationship to their commandments, the Three Traditions. Masquerade, Progeny and Diablarie. From the very beginning, the LeS aren't outright forbidding any of those... well, at least the first two, I can't remember details of the third.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Diablerie is strictly outlawed, because it destroys the soul and denies the victim an afterlife. None other than God should be allowed to pass judgement on one's soul. <i>According to the Lancea.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:04:40-07:00","id":965212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965026#post965026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And besides, the very same argument could be applied to the Lancea as well. They preach that it is their purpose to fulfill Satan's roll on earth. What better way to do that than to sign on with Belial's Brood, who believe that vampires are supposed to act like demons?</div> </div> </div> </div> A heretical Theban ritual from the Secrets of the Covenants Open Dev explicitly involves making a pact with s being called Belial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:56:25-07:00","id":965277,"title":"","content":"The idea that if someone's closer or not to Belial's Brood makes them unworthy of being cheered on is erroneous to begin with, I like Belial's Brood more than the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> That said, the covenants are different, and the core of the philosophies are, or were in first edition, not aligned. The Brood wouldn't be at home as a faction in the Circle any more than it would in the Lancea et Sanctum. If it happened, it would be a heretical sect in both cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:52:57-07:00","id":965307,"title":"","content":"I like the Brood too.<br /> <br /> You can play a Manananggal! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But still, if you're going to argue that they belong with the Circle just because they're blood mages, then I stand by my counter argument that they belong with the Lancea due to their ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T23:20:46-07:00","id":965516,"title":"","content":"You are more right than you think. As pointed above it seems we will have a sort of update of the Brood as a Lancea et Sanctum heresy in Secrets of the Covenants. Or something pretty close at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:21:23-07:00","id":965534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965516#post965516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are more right than you think. As pointed above it seems we will have a sort of update of the Brood as a Lancea et Sanctum heresy in Secrets of the Covenants. Or something pretty close at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little misleading. One mention of Belial in a Sanctified ritual is not the same thing as an update for the Brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:08:06-07:00","id":965550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That's a little misleading. One mention of Belial in a Sanctified ritual is not the same thing as an update for the Brood.</span> </div> </div> </div>I'm the serpent and the Father of Lies.<br /> <br /> <br /> More serious though, yeah, not an update perse, the Lancea et Sanctum chapter won't be Belial's Brood 2nd edition update, but is a nice alternative in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"use