ustom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T05:32:15-07:00","id":965616,"title":"","content":"Sadly, no. Stock photo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:27:57-07:00","id":965660,"title":"","content":"Belial's Brood was not covered in 2e for some reason that I can't remember. Maybe the Brood was a lie. It was a covenant that was a fractious collection of factions with varied beliefs. The largest six form the Hexad. The Brood are pagans as they are not Abrahamic, Dharmic, East Asian or one of the many minor religions that are excluded from paganism. One faction could be considered Abrahamic but would be considered blasphemous to the Lance. Another faction has methods which looks similar to the Lance so they would make for good heretics. As the thread was about the Circle, I don't see the relevance of Lance heretics but there you go. The other factions are not any more different than what the Circle accepts in 2e. The Brood never had Cruac and I don't know why they would want to join the Circle since they seem to just hide and lie to stay safe from the other covenants, but if they were inclined they should be accepted generally which does not mean in every domain because that is the way the Circle works, two factions could war with each other in a domain if they choose each claiming to be the true Circle. I guess the Brood would be heretics in the Circle except the notion of heresy in the Circle is blasphemy from &quot;they would probably inflict Final Death on anyone who tried to [impose a structured theology upon their followers and allies]&quot; The Brood certainly has some beliefs that would be unorthodox when viewed by most of the Circle. The Brood was the anti-Lance based on theology. Now the Circle is the anti-Lance based on underlying core beliefs. I don't know the Brood is necessary anymore except for the perks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:39:40-07:00","id":965665,"title":"","content":"I once made a comment about the LeS Belial ritual replacing the Brood, and got told &quot;no!&quot; by Rose, head Vamp developer. The Brood absolutely exist as its own entity, but its not really mentioned much with the different direction the game has taken (the strix focus).<br /> <br /> Given that the Bale Hounds and maeljin have likewise taken a very scarce-to-non-existant approach, I'm going to guess that the Inferno has something to do with it - pushing everything related to that a bit to the side. Possibly for its own 2e update, possibly because its being tied into something with Hunter / Lucifuge. I don't know much other than Inferno-style demon influece being saved for other things, or pushed to the side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:46:18-07:00","id":965671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965665#post965665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once made a comment about the LeS Belial ritual replacing the Brood, and got told &quot;no!&quot; by Rose, head Vamp developer. The Brood absolutely exist as its own entity, but its not really mentioned much with the different direction the game has taken (the strix focus).<br /> <br /> Given that the Bale Hounds and maeljin have likewise taken a very scarce-to-non-existant approach, I'm going to guess that the Inferno has something to do with it - pushing everything related to that a bit to the side. Possibly for its own 2e update, possibly because its being tied into something with Hunter / Lucifuge. I don't know much other than Inferno-style demon influece being saved for other things, or pushed to the side.</div> </div> </div> </div>WMG: It's for the Cross-over Chronicle - Inferno corrupts everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T09:25:52-07:00","id":965717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965660#post965660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Belial's Brood was not covered in 2e for some reason that I can't remember. Maybe the Brood was a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose has said lack of room. I'm inclined to believe her.<br /> <br /> The Circle and the Brood still have different goals, because the Circle is about more than 'not being like the Lancea et Sanctum,' and the Brood was never about that. The big difference in their belief system is that the Circle doesn't believe in losing all their Humanity, while the Brood does. The Brood believe, though this is putting it very simply, their vampirism is a shard of the Adversary that they're being blocked from embracing due to their humanity. Getting rid of all their humanity, embracing not just the Beast but what they believe to be its source, is their goal. Whereas the Circle believe their Embrace is a gift, and the Beast is a part of it. Abandoning oneself fully to it is as damning to the self as much as losing yourself completely to addiction would be as a living person. Their every step down the ladder of Humanity is meant to be fully appreciated, but one simply cannot do that at Humanity 0.<br /> <br /> It's true they have connections, as they are both a persecuted party, they follow pagan beliefs, though the Brood's are more in line with gnosticism, and stepping down the ladder is one aspect of their philosophy, but on their journey the Brood look eagerly ahead to becoming a native and putting their human existence behind them, while the Circle knows they can't appreciate their Gift without remaining a little like what the once were.<br /> <br /> If anything, the Brood is more like the strix, or more likely to follow them. But there's an added social component the strix lack and the strix encourage the abandoning of humanity the way the Beast does, not out of any embrace of something greater like the Brood, but because it's easy and feels good.<br /> <br /> Regarding the rite, I do think it's telling that there's a Theban sorcery ritual that offers service to Belial, considering Theban sorcery are granted to the Lance by Amoniel, who claims to be an angel of the Lord. But given what we know of Secrets of the Covenants, that it's based on the clanbook approach with fiction and mechanics that link up to it, I'd expect there to be at least one section if not focusing than involving Belial's Brood, perhaps reports from a Lancea et Sanctum Inquisitor seeking out a heretic who absconded with knowledge of the ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:49:13-07:00","id":965953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964835#post964835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To think that any (Covenants) are good or something to root for must be the result of some sort of bias. Covenants are bad, even though individual members are not...<br /> <br /> ...This was the intention. It's a horror game, not a dark superhero game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant interpretation! I like the cut of your jib, sir. I am picturing &quot;The Imperialists&quot; sub faction for the Invictus, forging colonial-stereotype -oppressive multi-domain empires, Brutal-Mao based Carthian in China, a Trans-human faction of Ordo that makes Nazi Germany's war-crime experiments on human subjects look tame, and an Inquisition style Lance sub-sect. I'll be using NPCs based in this Interpretation in my next game to drive home the point there is no objectively &quot;right/moral&quot; Covenant.<br /> <br /> I'll be starting another thread about other people's ideas for abhorrent sub-factions because I am genuinely interested but don't want to derail this lively discussion.--Link will go here as soon as I make the thread--","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-08-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:21:33-07:00","id":965962,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965953#post965953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brilliant interpretation! I like the cut of your jib, sir. I am picturing &quot;The Imperialists&quot; sub faction for the Invictus, forging colonial-stereotype -oppressive multi-domain empires, Brutal-Mao based Carthian in China, a Trans-human faction of Ordo that makes Nazi Germany's war-crime experiments on human subjects look tame, and an Inquisition style Lance sub-sect. I'll be using NPCs based in this Interpretation in my next game to drive home the point there is no objectively &quot;right/moral&quot; Covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anyone say a group had to be good or right to root for them?<br /> <br /> Ah, apparently atamajakki did.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible to root for the perceived bad guy. I doubt many people watch Dexter, House of Cards, Hannibal, Prison Break, Hustle, or Boardwalk Empire or any other shows thinking at the beginning of the episode, 'I sure hope they get them at the end tonight, this is horrible.' Though they may have thought it was horrible for other reasons than what the protagonist does.<br /> <br /> Just look at Dance Macabre. If your players have problems with the game as is, within that book the Invictus has the Prima Invicta, the Carthians the Commonwealth, the Ordo Dracul the Dragon's Eye, the Circle the Mother's Army, and the Lancea et Sanctum the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:51:31-07:00","id":965980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965665#post965665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once made a comment about the LeS Belial ritual replacing the Brood, and got told &quot;no!&quot; by Rose, head Vamp developer. The Brood absolutely exist as its own entity, but its not really mentioned much with the different direction the game has taken (the strix focus).<br /> <br /> Given that the Bale Hounds and maeljin have likewise taken a very scarce-to-non-existant approach, I'm going to guess that the Inferno has something to do with it - pushing everything related to that a bit to the side. Possibly for its own 2e update, possibly because its being tied into something with Hunter / Lucifuge. I don't know much other than Inferno-style demon influece being saved for other things, or pushed to the side.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong about this, but doesn't the Brood have a different recruitment method than any other covenant? I was told that vampires feel a subconscious calling that lures them into the Brood's fold. And unlike the other covenants, they'll let you walk away because anybody who does so ends up losing any memories regarding the Brood's secrets.<br /> <br /> So basically, they're a self sustaining covenant with a guaranteed insurance policy against traitors. Definitely sounds like something otherworldly is pulling the strings for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:01:37-07:00","id":965983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965980#post965980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong about this, but doesn't the Brood have a different recruitment method than any other covenant? I was told that vampires feel a subconscious calling that lures them into the Brood's fold. And unlike the other covenants, they'll let you walk away because anybody who does so ends up losing any memories regarding the Brood's secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's the Pursuit, very fun to role-play and you can back out by simply refusing to follow and nothing will come of it. Even once you join, most of the covenant doesn't care. The problem comes from Vaulderie, a group Vinculum and common practice among the Brood. If the Forsworn had a common blood bond with their covey, they may find it harder to let go. The sample fiction in the beginning of the book has an example of this.<br /> <br /> Either way you for the most part completely forget everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:42:20-07:00","id":966039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965983#post965983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's the Pursuit, very fun to role-play and you can back out by simply refusing to follow and nothing will come of it. Even once you join, most of the covenant doesn't care. The problem comes from Vaulderie, a group Vinculum and common practice among the Brood. If the Forsworn had a common blood bond with their covey, they may find it harder to let go. The sample fiction in the beginning of the book has an example of this.<br /> <br /> Either way you for the most part completely forget everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the bigger part of that is waking up one night, realizing you'd just lost five years of your requiem, and you now have ties to really demonic sons of btchs. And a few years down the line. you slowly realize you are the son of bitch from the past five years that terrorized the city. And they're gently pushing you to open the castle gates back up. Just let us in. Let us in. It's ok. It's totally cool. Those &quot;friends&quot; aren't your real friends anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:46:18-07:00","id":966041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965983#post965983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem comes from Vaulderie, a group Vinculum and common practice among the Brood.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahah! I knew it, they're the new Sabbat! I just had speculation until now.<br /> <br /> Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-09-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:08:01-07:00","id":966049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966039#post966039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bigger part of that is waking up one night, realizing you'd just lost five years of your requiem, and you now have ties to really demonic sons of btchs. And a few years down the line. you slowly realize you are the son of bitch from the past five years that terrorized the city. And they're gently pushing you to open the castle gates back up. Just let us in. Let us in. It's ok. It's totally cool. Those &quot;friends&quot; aren't your real friends anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was part of first edition, and the memories faded away similar to the Fog of Eternity vampires had while in torpor. But one of the ways you could start the process was by joining another covenant, keeping in mind that in first edition there was no mixing the way we sort of have now. The only memories that would be erased were those involving your Forsworn activities, including your demonic friends. If you had a blood bond you might feel a strange connection when someone pointed out the Roaring Serpent hooligan, but you wouldn't know who they were or likely even why.<br /> <br /> They'd know you, though.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> There are some similarities. But they are more philosophers of evil than the political combatants of the modern Sabbat. There's definitely overlap but they share some of that with the Followers of Set and the Lasombra. Vaulderie is one, but like a lot of Requiem, there's inspirations all around but it's for the most part unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:48:36-07:00","id":966072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966049#post966049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> There are some similarities. But they are more philosophers of evil than the political combatants of the modern Sabbat. There's definitely overlap but they share some of that with the Followers of Set and the Lasombra. Vaulderie is one, but like a lot of Requiem, there's inspirations all around but it's for the most part unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know that the covenants in Requiem aren't identical to Masquerade. But considering Invictus and Carthians are clearly meant to resemble Camarilla and Anarchs, I wondered if the Sabbat had managed to sneak in somehow. Seems like they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:24:44-07:00","id":966080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966049#post966049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was part of first edition, and the memories faded away similar to the Fog of Eternity vampires had while in torpor. But one of the ways you could start the process was by joining another covenant, keeping in mind that in first edition there was no mixing the way we sort of have now. The only memories that would be erased were those involving your Forsworn activities, including your demonic friends. If you had a blood bond you might feel a strange connection when someone pointed out the Roaring Serpent hooligan, but you wouldn't know who they were or likely even why.<br /> <br /> They'd know you, though.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> There are some similarities. But they are more philosophers of evil than the political combatants of the modern Sabbat. There's definitely overlap but they share some of that with the Followers of Set and the Lasombra. Vaulderie is one, but like a lot of Requiem, there's inspirations all around but it's for the most part unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the memories fade away. but that doesn't erase all the incidental evidence. Like all the gun runners were paid with your bank accounts. The signature calling card of the ripper is your solo violin. Your old warehouse was the site of horrible experimentation. Imagine you're new in town and you hear about this right bastard. and then all the evidence leads right to you. Are you still that guy? have you completely escape? Would you do it all over again? Can your friends trust you? Can you trust yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:37:30-07:00","id":966149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=964835#post964835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This was the intention. It's a horror game, not a dark superhero game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ya know, I missed this a while back, but I thought I'd toss something out. <br /> <br /> VtR 2e core book, page 7. &quot;Somebody cheated death to bring you back, and now you have to make up the debt. You can devote yourself to faith and good works. Play philanthropist. Play superhero. Or you can accept that you\u2019re damned and get the party started. Piss on the cross. Get some head. Little of both, probably.&quot;<br /> <br /> Acting like a superhero, confirmed part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T05:12:59-07:00","id":966154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966149#post966149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ya know, I missed this a while back, but I thought I'd toss something out.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e core book, page 7. &quot;Somebody cheated death to bring you back, and now you have to make up the debt. You can devote yourself to faith and good works. Play philanthropist. Play superhero. Or you can accept that you\u2019re damned and get the party started. Piss on the cross. Get some head. Little of both, probably.&quot;<br /> <br /> Acting like a superhero, confirmed part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> This little section right here may convince me to check out Requiem 2e then.<br /> <br /> As for the topic at hand, I always ran my 1e Requiem games as &quot;Dark Supers&quot; with a heroic Circle of the Crone and a villainous Lancea Sanctum (among other things that were Rule Zero'd into effect). Admittedly, part of this had to do with personal biases developed from my upbringing in a largely conservative Christian environment (and generally hating said environment), but part of it is because even in 1e, the Circle are portrayed as underdogs. And I like rooting for the underdog.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:37:35-07:00","id":966179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966149#post966149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ya know, I missed this a while back, but I thought I'd toss something out.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e core book, page 7. &quot;Somebody cheated death to bring you back, and now you have to make up the debt. You can devote yourself to faith and good works. Play philanthropist. Play superhero. Or you can accept that you\u2019re damned and get the party started. Piss on the cross. Get some head. Little of both, probably.&quot;<br /> <br /> Acting like a superhero, confirmed part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure you're being facetious, but still - no one's arguing against a particular story that explores heroic elements -<i> when it's balanced with the themes of being damned</i>. <br /> <br /> Your quote left out the preceding part. Note the theme is an equation: X + Y. Characters who think they can offset the curse by trying to be good guys, great. Players who just want to play vampire-themed superheroes, not my cup of vitae.<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <b>Piety + Blasphemy</b><br /> <br /> How did you get to be what you are? Were you a good girl, dragged kicking and screaming from heaven? Or a bad boy, brought back from the grave \u2019cause hell didn\u2019t deserve you?<br /> <br /> Little of both, probably.<br /> <br /> Somebody cheated death to bring you back, and now you have to make up the debt. You can devote yourself to faith and good works. Play philanthropist. Play superhero.<br /> <br /> Or you can accept that you\u2019re damned and get the party started. Piss on the cross. Get some head.<br /> <br /> Little of both, probably.<br /> ------------","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:37:13-07:00","id":966207,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why I left in the bit about damned, pissing, and sex. *shrugs* Covers the dark parts well enough.<br /> <br /> My point was part facetious, but also part serious. There's more than a bit of disdain for those who run the CofD games like superheroes on these forums. Its absolutely a valid playstyle, especially the darker aspects of being a superhero. Trying to suggest that it doesn't exist in the covenants is something I just flat out disagree with. Suggesting that it has to be subservant to &quot;damnation&quot; instead of working <i>with it</i> is also a pet peeve of mine. Its two sides of the same coin that work in conjunction. Vampires live in both the black and the white extremes, not comfortable greys. Just as you shouldn't forget the Blasphemy, you also shouldn't forget the Piety and goodworks that is absolutely part of the game and every covenant.<br /> <br /> To flip what you said, Holy, if people only playing vampire-themed superheroes isn't your cup of vitae, then neither are people only focused on vampire-themed nihlistic arsehulls. There are (at least) two sides to being a vampire, and each side is an entirely valid way of playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-09-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:57:41-07:00","id":966258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966207#post966207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To flip what you said, Holy, if people only playing vampire-themed superheroes isn't your cup of vitae, then neither are people only focused on vampire-themed nihlistic arsehulls. There are (at least) two sides to being a vampire, and each side is an entirely valid way of playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, it's the two great tastes that go great together. Both extremes feel off to me. It's just that my experience has been to see far more good-guys than complete-heels in games. I have some ideas on why that happens, but that's the pattern I have most often dealt with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:36:58-07:00","id":966278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966207#post966207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason why I left in the bit about damned, pissing, and sex. *shrugs* Covers the dark parts well enough.<br /> <br /> My point was part facetious, but also part serious. There's more than a bit of disdain for those who run the CofD games like superheroes on these forums. Its absolutely a valid playstyle, especially the darker aspects of being a superhero. Trying to suggest that it doesn't exist in the covenants is something I just flat out disagree with. Suggesting that it has to be subservant to &quot;damnation&quot; instead of working <i>with it</i> is also a pet peeve of mine. Its two sides of the same coin that work in conjunction. Vampires live in both the black and the white extremes, not comfortable greys. Just as you shouldn't forget the Blasphemy, you also shouldn't forget the Piety and goodworks that is absolutely part of the game and every covenant.<br /> <br /> To flip what you said, Holy, if people only playing vampire-themed superheroes isn't your cup of vitae, then neither are people only focused on vampire-themed nihlistic arsehulls. There are (at least) two sides to being a vampire, and each side is an entirely valid way of playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWell said, my friend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:40:49-07:00","id":966387,"title":"","content":"The &quot;easy&quot; part is what said the Circle had to be good guys. There were great answers as to why someone would root for the Circle of the Crone. However, that was not the question. If it is easy to root for someone broadly then we are not talking in certain situations. It can be easy to root for Lecter versus Childers because Childers is a dick. It should not be easy to root for Lecter when he is trying to get an innocent family murdered. So the phrasing of the question suggested the Circle are good guys or the other covenants must be so much worse than the Circle appears to be the good guys. There was nothing wrong with the question but I don't agree with the premise suggested by it. It switches the game from horror to dark superhero so I mentioned that.<br /> <br /> Any kind of superhero can be played in a horror game. A character does not change the nature of a game. All the covenants are bad guys with positive qualities. Vampires could be viewed in the same way as a group, probably more positive than any of the covenants too. These are views consistent with horror. Horror does not mean the absence of good. Good does not dominate in a horror game, it is subdued or challenged by the more prevalent bad. In this context, the Circle must be part of the bad because it is still large, a set piece. Because this is a game, however, parts of the Circle should not be bad. This is true of all the covenants. Whether the good part encompasses the players or their faction or the entire group they belong in the immediate setting, does not change the covenant when looked at broadly.<br /> <br /> Players could try to change the covenant as a whole like some kind of superhero but they should ultimately fail. That is horror. Making the world a better place belongs in a superhero game. Trying to make the world a better place has no genre. I think everyone here gets this. Hope this shows I do too.<br /> <br /> *I actually thought lack of space to do Belial's Broos properly was what Rose had said, but I wasn't going to risk putting words in her mouth because it was years ago and I wasn't going to try to find it either. Too lazy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-09-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:09:27-07:00","id":966695,"title":"","content":"Ehhh.<br /> <br /> I'm on board with saying there's nothing preventing superhero stuff in Vampire. As in &quot;horror&quot; allowing characters to try making the world a better place but never succeeding. I want to disagree, but at the same time it's kind of how I tend to run my games soooo yeah. Well, still, I usually grant some form of change to my players. Usually, for the better, but never ideal. The first game I ran that lasted three years saw the city they were in go from a pretty stable cold war situation to a power vacuum to a tense resolution to full on invasion/civil war to actual apparent stability when the big threat was neutralized. The state the city was in when the game ended was kind of okay mostly and the players agreed that at least the prince was someone they could bargain with and was probably the most qualified even though he's invictus and they weren't invictus fans.<br /> <br /> The current game I'm running is... well, the premise is very removed from your typical Requiem game. We're almost finished and the players are heading towards a very big change that is good for them and most of the people (vampires) they know but has some repercussions they might not yet realize and some they definitely don't realize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T05:08:27-07:00","id":966715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966387#post966387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It switches the game from horror to dark superhero so I mentioned that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again with this premesis. You're commenting about the phrasing of the opening question. Now here's a comment about your phrasing - you are creating a false dichotomy here, that somehow Horror and dark superhero must be mutually exclusive genres or types of games. Vampire can be both. There is nothing wrong with VtR being run as a dark superhero game if that's what the troupe wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the covenants are bad guys with positive qualities. </div> </div> </div> No. The only flat out &quot;bad guys&quot; in Requiem are the strix, everything else is a question of individuals. Covenants are portrayed as monstrous, but in the CofD, monster does not equal &quot;bad guy.&quot; There's good and bad involved in any organization, and vampire organizations are no different. Shades of grey and moral questions are the rule here.<br /> <br /> Yeah, covenants in the Vampire core were portrayed at their worst. That doesn't make them bad organizations. Its just where the spotlight was shining at the given moment. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Players could try to change the covenant as a whole like some kind of superhero but they should ultimately fail. That is horror. Making the world a better place belongs in a superhero game. Trying to make the world a better place has no genre. I think everyone here gets this. Hope this shows I do too. </div> </div> </div> The only difference between &quot;trying&quot; and &quot;making&quot; the world a better place is if a given plan succeed or not - and no matter the genre, you will have plans that succeed as intended at some point. That's simply how storytelling works - very few people like watching characters fail every time, there needs to be triumphs as well. As well, no matter the genre, there will be failures - not many people like infailable, invincible characters.<br /> <br /> And, no, I don't &quot;get this&quot; because I just flat out disagree with you. You're drawing arbitrary distinctions here. <i>That's the problem. The world does not exist in binary</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> I swear, this is like some kind of &quot;gamer bias&quot; or something. There's this subtle undercurrent of disdain for bringing in &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; to the point that people use it as an insult to shout down arguments. This can be in any of the CofD (or WoD) games. The word &quot;superhero&quot; is used as a derogatory term to shut down completely valid styles of play. Its seen as &quot;dirty&quot; somehow, an undesirable. I've seen the term used to shout down someone making an argument when their argument had nothing to do with superheroics. Mind, the argument was a bit gonzo, and I think it was a bad argument, but there was no reason to shout it down by saying &quot;superhero&quot; when it had nothing to do with the superhero genre. This disdain or dislike seems to be rooted in some kind of &quot;horror purist&quot; mentality, where there's a Right Way and a Wrong Way to run the games.<br /> <br /> Well, f@#$ that. Every table is different, and if someone wants to run their games that way, they not only should, but <i>there is ample support in the books for it.</i> Genres aren't pigeon holes. There are no hard lines between fantasy, science fiction, supernatural horror, superheroics and murder mysteries. Is a story about a witch solving crime a Mystery novel or a Fantasy one? If you look across bookshelves, you'll find such books in both areas. Rather than boxes, genres are more like ingredients. All CofD &quot;dishes&quot; come with &quot;fantasy,&quot; &quot;mystery&quot; and &quot;horror&quot; as ingredients by default. Romance is a common spice. Superheroism is another. Adding more ingredients does not change that its still a horror story. It changes the flavor, but that's a good thing, since everyone can flavor their games to their tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:24:23-07:00","id":966767,"title":"","content":"Every table is unique. No game is monolothic and completely pure around a single theme. I don't see anyone arguing against that concept, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> .<br /> <br /> But come on. If my table is deciding on running a game and we are looking between Champions, Vampire, and Dungeons and Dragons - I would never in a million years tell a new player not familiar with any of them - &quot;Oh, they're all superhero games.&quot; Or all Fantasy. Or all horror.<br /> <br /> Or describe a romantic comedy as a horror movie because there was a jump scare bit in it. Etc.<br /> <br /> Genres exist. They aren't binary, you're absolutely right. They get peppered in with other concepts (low fantasy, high fantasy), or merged (dark comedy, dramedy). Or specifically messed with to try and make something both sci-fi and fantasy (Spelljammer). Or actively a-genre and just a neutral system (GURPS core).<br /> <br /> Vampire is not a-genre. Vampire is a game of personal horror. Any table can sprinkle anything they want into any game they want. There's no Onyx Path police that are going to come and take away your books for 'playing wrong.'<br /> <br /> The frustration for me, and I suspect others, is that it can be difficult when forming a game - either in pick-up groups, or under inexperienced troupes, or less socially savvy groups - when people come in with wildly different expectations of what the core genre is. Not every table is lucky or experienced enough to be able to settle these differences with a social contract. And so when it seems a person is completely ignoring the personal horror aspect of Vampire, it can cause problems.<br /> <br /> It's totally okay to tell someone who shows up with Deadpool as a character concept to your Requiem game that their character may be better suited for Champions. And you can do it without making them feel like crap about it or that their preferences don't matter.<br /> <br /> I'll even agree that some people pull out the superhero comparison too quickly or on unrelated issues. That doesn't make the overall point wrong: Vampire has a particular problem with genre-shift away from what a lot of people consider personal horror toward what a lot of people consider superheroics. <br /> <br /> &quot;I want to play a Blood and Smoke game without any personal horror,&quot; - is a valid feeling for anyone or any table, but I think it's pretty clearly veering off into different territories than the book. While - &quot;I want to play a Blood and Smoke game without any Superheroes/Stampunk/Zombies/Romance.&quot; - is still pretty covered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:16:39-07:00","id":966787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966767#post966767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That doesn't make the overall point wrong: Vampire has a particular problem with genre-shift away from what a lot of people consider personal horror toward what a lot of people consider superheroics.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, there are people who have a problem with conflicting playstyles. That is a different matter. Its no different than a variation on &quot;role&quot; play versus &quot;roll&quot; play arguments that come up. Everyone has their own taste, and they are all valid. If there's a problem? Its that you have players who don't want to play the same style as the ST. That's not the problem of the players for wanting to be &quot;superheroics.&quot; <br /> <br /> If someone is coming to your game and doesn't udnerstand the book, possibly because they haven't read it, or because they have different expectations from previous games, that's a sign of a different issue at play - RPGs have their roots in war games, after all. Its not easy to break away from that mentality. And it has nothing to do with superheroes. <br /> <br /> And, most importantly, the use of your overall point. You want to avoid the extreme of &quot;superhero&quot; characters. The problem is that people are using that label to try and push to the other extreme, and that's just as much of a problem. Vampire is a game of mixing the two extremes together.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I want to play a Blood and Smoke game without any personal horror,&quot; </div> </div> </div> I return your words to you. No one is arguing for that concept, Holy. That's all on you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While - &quot;I want to play a Blood and Smoke game without any Superheroes/Stampunk/Zombies/Romance.&quot; - is still pretty covered. </div> </div> </div> Hmm.... Game of sex and murder... humans are your dates... shadow crossed lovers... entire clan devoted to emotional dependacy... are you <i>really really </i>sure that asking for a Requiem 2e game without Romance is standard, like you're implying? <br /> <br /> As for zombies? Ha! Theban ritual for making zombies. Revenants and dragur are effectively zombies by another name. Animalism 2 creates a zombie animal. Strix are evil-spirit possessed undead zombie-bodies. VtR is lousy with zombies. Hells, the Gangrel clan book even covered draugr-based zombie swarms. The Kindred cover a lot of different kinds of undead under the &quot;vampire&quot; umbrella.<br /> <br /> Steam punk.... well, even the Ordo doesn't really touch steam punk, but the romance of the Victorian-era mad scientists with an alchemical focus? That's a yes. <br /> <br /> I dont think games without these themes are as well covered as you are implying them to be, Holy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:56:30-07:00","id":966802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966767#post966767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I want to play a Blood and Smoke game without any personal horror,&quot; - is a valid feeling for anyone or any table, but I think it's pretty clearly veering off into different territories than the book. While - &quot;I want to play a Blood and Smoke game without any Superheroes/Stampunk/Zombies/Romance.&quot; - is still pretty covered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The world needs more people like you! Articulate people who can explain and acknowledge the complexities of reality without sliding into headlong into relativism so deep that we abandon memetic technologies like the concepts of definition, destinction, and genre.<br /> <br /> To my way of thinking that type of rudderless relativism that your post frames into a clear perspective is regressive and a destructive extremity of the post-modern mindset. Gaming is a storytelling art, distinct from literature but with many paralells, and post-modern art ideas of abandoning any notion of standards of what is acceptable as an archaic relic of chauvinism doesn't respect the truth that some things are better than others, which we've all experienced in our lives and know to be accurate. Some things are better that others and admitting that as a basis for creating standards it isn't necessarily archaic or chauvinistic. Trading craftsmanship, discipline, and elegant design within standards for edginess, and sloppy work <i>without artistic integrity</i>* is hurting the gaming art form as it is hurting other types of art.<br /> <br /> While your whole post was amazing and very insightful, I chose the last sentence because it nicely frames all this in context of Vampire. Also it seems to be the part most disected by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> and I wanted you to know that I understood your previous text made it clear you acknowledged that all the little bits exist in the setting as motifs, minor themes, or simply occasional props or scenery within a vampire game and that you were talking about the primary focus. I guess the best metaphor is cinematography for camera angles, framing, music score, lighting and cuts extablish the genre just as much as what is happening in front of the camera and that is the same as the Storyteller's focus and intent. Whether things are in the movie matter less than if and how they are focused on in the move.<br /> <br /> *Disclaimer: Felt that phrase needed explaining in context of gaming because it is meant to also cover art in general - instead of fair arbitration based on careful understanding of the Chronicle a Storyteller is running (the setting the Soryteller created with intention and care, in the system the Storyteller chose to customize to make it come alive and be consistent) the Storyteller caves into requests which mar the Chronicle due to emotional factors like fear of rejection or peer pressure like giving up to being hounded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-10-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:20:51-07:00","id":966809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966787#post966787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, there are people who have a problem with conflicting playstyles. That is a different matter. Its no different than a variation on &quot;role&quot; play versus &quot;roll&quot; play arguments that come up. Everyone has their own taste, and they are all valid. If there's a problem? Its that you have players who don't want to play the same style as the ST. That's not the problem of the players for wanting to be &quot;superheroics.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a need to separate the concept of conflicting play-styles from conflicting genre-styles. I see them as part of the same overall package.<br /> <br /> And like, I don't see how to get around the fact that when someone asks me, &quot;Hey - I want to do a LARP this weekend. I see there's a NERO game and MES game on Friday. What's the gist on those?&quot;<br /> <br /> My response is, &quot;NERO's a high-fantasy boffer LARP, MES is vampire horror/politics.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not going to bother to say, &quot;Well, actually, genre itself is an abstract concept with no hard-drawn lines or definitions, so in essence both games are exactly anything you want them to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone is coming to your game and doesn't udnerstand the book, possibly because they haven't read it, or because they have different expectations from previous games, that's a sign of a different issue at play - RPGs have their roots in war games, after all. Its not easy to break away from that mentality. And it has nothing to do with superheroes. </div> </div> </div>This is exactly my point. I look at it like accents. The first game you learn to roleplay in, naturally colors the next game you try. When you play with a lot of people, you start to notice similar patterns. A hardcore D&amp;D player brings in different concepts and playstyles than a die-hard Monsterhearts fan who brings in different concepts than a Warhammer miniatures gal. What it has to do with superheroes, is that those particular themes seem especially prone to coming into Vampire games at the expense of personal horror. People have noticed that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, most importantly, the use of your overall point. You want to avoid the extreme of &quot;superhero&quot; characters. The problem is that people are using that label to try and push to the other extreme, and that's just as much of a problem. Vampire is a game of mixing the two extremes together. </div> </div> </div>And here I think you are knee-jerking. If a mixed drink is supposed to have half coke and half rum, if you find out it's 75% rum, you either start adding more coke, or somehow start subtracting the rum. If you're just looking at the change - yes, it looks like - oh, my god - you're just moving to the other extreme of all coke! But that's only if they <i>never stop</i> adding/subtracting.<br /> <br /> If a game is out of balance, and you believe there are too many superheroics and not enough personal horror, what is your advice on fixing that balance? What I'm saying is you either focus less on superheroics, or focus more on personal horror. It works for the reverse too. If you feel your game is all nihilistic arseholes with no themes of redemption or humanity, etc. What is your solution other than focusing on redemption, or moving away from more nihilism?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm.... Game of sex and murder... humans are your dates... shadow crossed lovers... entire clan devoted to emotional dependacy... are you <i>really really </i>sure that asking for a Requiem 2e game without Romance is standard, like you're implying?<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> I don't think games without these themes are as well covered as you are implying them to be, Holy. </div> </div> </div>I am <i>really</i>, <i>really </i>sure, yes. If I had to keep one aspect in a vampire game, it would be personal horror. It wouldn't be dependent romance, it would't be steam punk, it wouldn't be wizards or orcs or zombies. I think it would be far easier to drop those latter concepts than the former. That's what I'm arguing.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing they can't have a place, or be interesting, or be worked into things in creative ways, or that if someone wants to run a mutant superhero chronicle they couldn't find some way to do it and support it with a mechanic or fluff from some book in the Vampire universe.<br /> <br /> But if I'm running a one shot for my friends, and I tell them - just let me know what genre: If they tell me they want to play a superhero game, I'm gonna grab Marvel or Champions, not Blood and Smoke. If they tell me they want to play Stark Trek game, I'd feel a little weird running a Masquerade game where one of the pre-fabs was a Malkavian Trekkie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 09-10-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:12:34-07:00","id":966945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum#post958806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Studying Cruac tends to Erode a vampires Humanity., studying Theban sorcery, forced him to grudgingly struggle to maintain his humanity<br /> <br /> The Circle Flouts societal conventions.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum generally upholds them<br /> <br /> why, given all of this, is it so easy to root for the Circle?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, all the Covenants have an evil side. Its a horror game and this is by design. That said, if you find yourself routing for a particular covenant its probably because of your own bias. I like the Order just because of Dracula and Science (I'm a nerd but shhh, don't tell anyone). Everything from Dragon knights to supernatural investigators, theres so many roleplaying ideas to run with that you can easily have completely different games based within the Ordo Dracul. That said, theres plenty that can erode a vampires humanity while being in the Order and many ways to view it as inhuman and evil.<br /> <br /> I suspect if you like the idea of flouting societal conventions and being the underdog, the circle will appeal to you. I find that both religious convenants turn off a lot of players for one of two reasons. 1) They are Agnostic/Atheist and don't like the religious aspect of these convenants 2) They are religious and don't like the connections to real religions these convenants have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=960288#post960288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an athiest with no love for religion of any kind, I totally dig the Sanctified, and as much as I want to appreciate the Crones... and they do have some cool things... they just fall flat for me overall.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason I like the Caine mythology of VtM. Of course it's all crap, but as a work of fiction, Christianity is just more compelling to me than paganism, and fits the vampire theme of damnation so well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much my view as well. I like the idea of vampires being cursed by god. Its dark, its edgy, its straight out of hot topic. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:12:17-07:00","id":967065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966149#post966149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acting like a superhero, confirmed part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you're a super hero, then the Lancea Sanctum would be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spectre_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">The Spectre</a>. (Why is he even in the Justice League? He is basically living proof that it's okay for heroes to torture criminals before horrifically killing them!)<br /> <br /> <br /> But on the topic of super heroes, I think that might draw too much attention to the masquerade. If criminals and evil doers are getting handled before the police even arrive, and those criminals keep swearing their attackers were like something out of a comic book, then eventually a story is going to end up on the news, which attracts unwanted attention. Even rumors about superhuman events could attract government agencies and hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-10-2016, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:22:31-07:00","id":967117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966809#post966809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a need to separate the concept of conflicting play-styles from conflicting genre-styles. I see them as part of the same overall package.</div> </div> </div> </div> And that's the heart of my problem. They're not. They're completely different things. Conflicting playstyles refers to players not able to game together because they want different things out of the game and play characters in ways that clash, and not have fun together. Conflicting genre styles (pretending for a moment that such thing exists, I don't think it does) happens at the meta-game level and chronicle planning by the ST, no player involvment necessary. For the record, a large part of my point is that superheroes and personal horror are not naturally conflicting story types. In fact, I will argue that personal horror is rather central to most superhero stories.<br /> <br /> In short, my point is that its not the style of the game that's the problem, its the players not meshing together. Blaming it on a genre is misleading. Using a genre as a way to shout down people that enjoy that style game (and, yes, there are successful Vampire games run in that style) is bad taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And here I think you are knee-jerking. </div> </div> </div> Actually, I'm trying to point out something indictive of human nature. Humans tend towards extremes, not balance. You reject one extreme, you will naturally gravitate to the other instead of reaching a balance point. Its part of the reason nature always appears in cycles, rising and falling, instead of stasis at a single point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a game is out of balance, and you believe there are too many superheroics and not enough personal horror, what is your advice on fixing that balance? </div> </div> </div> My advice is &quot;what is most fun for the players and ST involved?&quot; As long as the mix is fun for those involved, its not an issue. Acknowledging that others tables prefer different ratio, hells, different ingredients than your table is also good. You don't want superheroes at your table? Fine. That's your perogative. But its not fair to say they don't belong in the game at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am <i>really</i>, <i>really </i>sure, yes. If I had to keep one aspect in a vampire game, it would be personal horror. It wouldn't be dependent romance, it would't be steam punk, it wouldn't be wizards or orcs or zombies. I think it would be far easier to drop those latter concepts than the former. That's what I'm arguing. </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking you to drop anything. Rather, I'm pointing out that Vampire is all these things by default. Which is my argument from the beginning. Dropping everything out but &quot;personal horror&quot; is reductive and an inacurate depictation of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:03:57-07:00","id":967168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=967117#post967117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And that's the heart of my problem. They're not. They're completely different things. Conflicting playstyles refers to players not able to game together because they want different things out of the game and play characters in ways that clash, and not have fun together. Conflicting genre styles (pretending for a moment that such thing exists, I don't think it does) happens at the meta-game level and chronicle planning by the ST, no player involvment necessary. For the record, a large part of my point is that superheroes and personal horror are not naturally conflicting story types. In fact, I will argue that personal horror is rather central to most superhero stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one person hears 'Fantasy Genre' and thinks Harry Potter, while a second thinks Warhammer Fantasy - those are conflicting styles. If you don't like the term, fine. But yeah, we'll agree to disagree here. If you honestly believe there is no point to distinct genres, that it's only a problem in the STs head, and not viewpoints that players also bring to the table, then we're talking past each other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short, my point is that its not the style of the game that's the problem, its the players not meshing together. Blaming it on a genre is misleading. Using a genre as a way to shout down people that enjoy that style game (and, yes, there are successful Vampire games run in that style) is bad taste. </div> </div> </div>Again, rehashing points already agreed to. I don't support anyone who tells you your game is bad. I'm not blaming the concept of 'genre' on the issue that I'm trying to discuss: That it's common practice for some kinds of players to ignore the Darkness in the 'Chronicles of Darkness' game, and instead basically just play superheores with Vampire-themed superpowers, while ignoring or running away from the (I think most people will agree are more important) personal horror aspects.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry you or your games may have been shouted down in the past. I definitely apologize if I ever did that personally. <br /> <br /> But even if I did, that doesn't take away at all from my above point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I'm trying to point out something indictive of human nature. Humans tend towards extremes, not balance. You reject one extreme, you will naturally gravitate to the other instead of reaching a balance point. Its part of the reason nature always appears in cycles, rising and falling, instead of stasis at a single point. </div> </div> </div>This has no bearing on the discussion. An interesting tidbit of philosophy, which I also think is wrong, but has no bearing on whether Vampire is more of a superhero game or a horror game at its core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My advice is &quot;what is most fun for the players and ST involved?&quot; As long as the mix is fun for those involved, its not an issue. Acknowledging that others tables prefer different ratio, hells, different ingredients than your table is also good. You don't want superheroes at your table? Fine. That's your perogative. But its not fair to say they don't belong in the game at all. </div> </div> </div>First, you're changing the premise. My question was about a game that was out of balance. If it wasn't out of balance, then the question wouldn't have been asked. But for those games where personal horror is lacking, you either add more of it, or take out whatever else is replacing it. If it ain't broke, don't fix it is absolutely valid. But when people come in asking why their web-slinging wise-cracking vigilante Gangrel was denied by their local ST - fair advice is to say, 'Maybe make less of a super-hero. Try to add some nuance, play up the horrific aspects.' Saying, 'Find a game where the ST likes it' is also fair advice, if that's an option, but it doesn't invalidate the other advice in any way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not asking you to drop anything. Rather, I'm pointing out that Vampire is all these things by default. Which is my argument from the beginning. Dropping everything out but &quot;personal horror&quot; is reductive and an inacurate depictation of the game. </div> </div> </div>You must get angry at bookstores a lot. How dare they label all of these books as 'Romance' - don't they know how reductive and inaccurate that description is? Any one of these books is so much more.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the discussion, MCN - but I think we clearly see we aren't going to reach a meeting of the minds on this. : )<br /> <br /> I'll end my piece with a quote from the book itself. You might read this and take away the idea that Vampire is a spectrum where anything can happen. I agree, but I <b>also </b>see an attempt to set a tone and theme, and feel absolutely comfortable letting people know when I think their personal concepts have missed that tone/themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vampire </b>is a game of visceral drama and personal horror.<br /> <b>Vampire </b>is about sex and murder, about power and wild defiance. It\u2019s about urban squalor and the romance of the city. It\u2019s about what\u2019s wrong with you \u2014 yes, you \u2014 and how that shapes the monster you\u2019ll become.<br /> <b>Vampire </b>is also about thrilling action and nail-biting paranoia. It\u2019s about dying young and being a great-looking corpse. It\u2019s about acting out in all of the ways we imagine we would, if only we couldn\u2019t see ourselves in the mirror.<br /> <b>Vampire </b>is a game about dead people and it should make you feel alive.<br /> <b>Vampire </b>is built on contrast, taking place in a World of Darkness with blinding whites and pitch blacks. Characters try to stay in the cool, comfortable grays, but they can\u2019t hide all the time. And, hey, they look good in black. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:38:39-07:00","id":967527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966787#post966787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, there are people who have a problem with conflicting playstyles. That is a different matter. Its no different than a variation on &quot;role&quot; play versus &quot;roll&quot; play arguments that come up. Everyone has their own taste, and they are all valid. If there's a problem? Its that you have players who don't want to play the same style as the ST. That's not the problem of the players for wanting to be &quot;superheroics.&quot;<br /> <br /> If someone is coming to your game and doesn't udnerstand the book, possibly because they haven't read it, or because they have different expectations from previous games, that's a sign of a different issue at play - RPGs have their roots in war games, after all. Its not easy to break away from that mentality. And it has nothing to do with superheroes.<br /> <br /> And, most importantly, the use of your overall point. You want to avoid the extreme of &quot;superhero&quot; characters. The problem is that people are using that label to try and push to the other extreme, and that's just as much of a problem. Vampire is a game of mixing the two extremes together.<br /> I return your words to you. No one is arguing for that concept, Holy. That's all on you.<br /> <br /> Hmm.... Game of sex and murder... humans are your dates... shadow crossed lovers... entire clan devoted to emotional dependacy... are you <i>really really </i>sure that asking for a Requiem 2e game without Romance is standard, like you're implying?<br /> <br /> As for zombies? Ha! Theban ritual for making zombies. Revenants and dragur are effectively zombies by another name. Animalism 2 creates a zombie animal. Strix are evil-spirit possessed undead zombie-bodies. VtR is lousy with zombies. Hells, the Gangrel clan book even covered draugr-based zombie swarms. The Kindred cover a lot of different kinds of undead under the &quot;vampire&quot; umbrella.<br /> <br /> Steam punk.... well, even the Ordo doesn't really touch steam punk, but the romance of the Victorian-era mad scientists with an alchemical focus? That's a yes.<br /> <br /> I dont think games without these themes are as well covered as you are implying them to be, Holy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think that Vampire without personal horror... Something I've tried to do is to &quot;Decamp&quot; CWOD And that is , all by itself, difficult enough.<br /> <br /> With things like &quot;Bane in a burger&quot; and TV shows designed to send subliminal messages to brainwash people into being apathetic zombies... ook the last is pretty close to real life, but you see my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:52:56-07:00","id":967537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=967527#post967527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that Vampire without personal horror... Something I've tried to do is to &quot;Decamp&quot; CWOD And that is , all by itself, difficult enough.<br /> <br /> With things like &quot;Bane in a burger&quot; and TV shows designed to send subliminal messages to brainwash people into being apathetic zombies... ook the last is pretty close to real life, but you see my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bane Burger. and so the Vegan Vampires over run us all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:44:24-07:00","id":967570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=961863#post961863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is the actual answer to the OP's question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah guys, come on, I got this! :P<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:49:55-07:00","id":970927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=965717#post965717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rose has said lack of room. I'm inclined to believe her.<br /> <br /> The Circle and the Brood still have different goals, because the Circle is about more than 'not being like the Lancea et Sanctum,' and the Brood was never about that. The big difference in their belief system is that the Circle doesn't believe in losing all their Humanity, while the Brood does. The Brood believe, though this is putting it very simply, their vampirism is a shard of the Adversary that they're being blocked from embracing due to their humanity. Getting rid of all their humanity, embracing not just the Beast but what they believe to be its source, is their goal. Whereas the Circle believe their Embrace is a gift, and the Beast is a part of it. Abandoning oneself fully to it is as damning to the self as much as losing yourself completely to addiction would be as a living person. Their every step down the ladder of Humanity is meant to be fully appreciated, but one simply cannot do that at Humanity 0.<br /> <br /> It's true they have connections, as they are both a persecuted party, they follow pagan beliefs, though the Brood's are more in line with gnosticism, and stepping down the ladder is one aspect of their philosophy, but on their journey the Brood look eagerly ahead to becoming a native and putting their human existence behind them, while the Circle knows they can't appreciate their Gift without remaining a little like what the once were.<br /> <br /> If anything, the Brood is more like the strix, or more likely to follow them. But there's an added social component the strix lack and the strix encourage the abandoning of humanity the way the Beast does, not out of any embrace of something greater like the Brood, but because it's easy and feels good.<br /> <br /> Regarding the rite, I do think it's telling that there's a Theban sorcery ritual that offers service to Belial, considering Theban sorcery are granted to the Lance by Amoniel, who claims to be an angel of the Lord. But given what we know of Secrets of the Covenants, that it's based on the clanbook approach with fiction and mechanics that link up to it, I'd expect there to be at least one section if not focusing than involving Belial's Brood, perhaps reports from a Lancea et Sanctum Inquisitor seeking out a heretic who absconded with knowledge of the ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Another line I've used a time or two, to summarize the Circles Views on their Humanity<br /> <br /> &quot;Our humanity is Infinitely precious, that is what makes it fitting as a sacrifice to the gods&quot; <br /> <br /> I could see them in that context being offended by the broods deliberate treating humanity as something unwanted and unneeded the Circle SACRIFICES humanity<br /> <br /> The brood treats it as a prison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:20:06-07:00","id":971137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=966039#post966039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the bigger part of that is waking up one night, realizing you'd just lost five years of your requiem, and you now have ties to really demonic sons of btchs. And a few years down the line. you slowly realize you are the son of bitch from the past five years that terrorized the city. And they're gently pushing you to open the castle gates back up. Just let us in. Let us in. It's ok. It's totally cool. Those &quot;friends&quot; aren't your real friends anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThat was actually the plot of my first chronicle when Requiem came out in 04 way before they explained that aspect of the brood. Strange Minds. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:10:47-07:00","id":972149,"title":"","content":"This thread has been very helpful in helping me look at the lancea et sanctum in a better light. Its sad to say but at character creation all of my players quickly passed on the covenant due to cultural and historical bias, seeing it only as the 'chuch covenant'. Also, a lot of it is my fault as due to same bias i feel i did not 'sale' the covenant properly enough. <br /> <br /> In my game, at this point, i feel that one of my player's character could develop into something that is in line with the LS. I think that by toning down the aspect of zealotry and putting more light on the creed of making a ''better'' world (particularly the aspect of protecting the innocent with a little of punishing the wicked) , i could at least have the player consider have his character join the covenant as a possibility. The whole sermon and zealotry aspects could be presented much later. Of course the goal is not to make the character join the covenant but to to present the Lancea as an option that is as valid as the other covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T00:06:44-07:00","id":972373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=972149#post972149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has been very helpful in helping me look at the lancea et sanctum in a better light. Its sad to say but at character creation all of my players quickly passed on the covenant due to cultural and historical bias, seeing it only as the 'chuch covenant'. Also, a lot of it is my fault as due to same bias i feel i did not 'sale' the covenant properly enough.<br /> <br /> In my game, at this point, i feel that one of my player's character could develop into something that is in line with the LS. I think that by toning down the aspect of zealotry and putting more light on the creed of making a ''better'' world (particularly the aspect of protecting the innocent with a little of punishing the wicked) , i could at least have the player consider have his character join the covenant as a possibility. The whole sermon and zealotry aspects could be presented much later. Of course the goal is not to make the character join the covenant but to to present the Lancea as an option that is as valid as the other covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be honest, the Lancea Sanctum is the 'church covenant.' It's just a version of the church that never adapted to religious reform policies and still believes nailing criminals to crosses is an acceptable form of punishment. They are, for lack of a better term, a Christian variety of Islamic extremism. So when you think about it from that perspective, it's easy to see how people might take offense to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2016, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T02:42:06-07:00","id":972419,"title":"","content":"Except they aren't Christian since they don't observe any of the tenets of Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:11:09-07:00","id":973081,"title":"","content":"That's kind of splitting hairs, imho. The Lance might technically not be Christian, but they absolutely are inspired by Christianity (esepcially Roman Catholicism), and that association is enough for most people. They're definitely the Corrupt Church archetype. Granted, in the CofD, ALL churches are pretty much &quot;corrupt&quot; because God is pretty much a lie - either a tyranical symbol in a supernal world of occult symbolism, a giant tyrannical machine, or some other powerful supernatural, such as one of the Judges or a powerful Keroberus or the like.<br /> <br /> Of course, its not like any other religion is right at this point either, subject to the same &quot;powerful evil overlord&quot; stance. And even the Ordo Dracul's science is pretty terrible - unlike mundane sceince, which produces knowledge and technology that can spread and improve the lives of the many, Coils improve the individual and not the whole, leading to more corruption in the hands of the few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-20-2016, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:33:44-07:00","id":973091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=973081#post973081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even the Ordo Dracul's science is pretty terrible - unlike mundane sceince, which produces knowledge and technology that can spread and improve the lives of the many, Coils improve the individual and not the whole, leading to more corruption in the hands of the few.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liked your analysis of CofD religions but I do believe you are looking at science both in game and out of game through<a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Rose-Colored_Mirrorshades\" target=\"_blank\"> r</a><a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Rose-Colored_Mirrorshades\" target=\"_blank\">ose-tinted mirrorshades</a> (Two internet Points for those that know the reference without clicking the link). Coils have never produced anything as horrific as the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969630-can-other-great-apes-become-awakened?p=970958#post970958\">atomic bomb</a>, weaponized anthrax, mass-produced mustard gas, high-explosive or white phosphorous artillery, inter-continental missiles, biased research paid for by interested businesses to inspire consumers to buy things that actually harm them (like tobacco historically, or sports drinks currently) and wide spread eugenics (as practiced in Nazi Germany). This doesn't even mention the shadowy corners of fictionalized science within CofD, nor the horrors that exist in the real world but are simply not public knowledge.<br /> <br /> Science and religions are tools and as tools can be wielded for great good or great harm.<br /> <br /> Your exact argument that Coils are smaller in scale is what limits the damage and evil they are capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-20-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T08:28:11-07:00","id":973152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=973091#post973091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liked your analysis of CofD religions but I do believe you are looking at science both in game and out of game through<a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Rose-Colored_Mirrorshades\" target=\"_blank\"> r</a><a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Rose-Colored_Mirrorshades\" target=\"_blank\">ose-tinted mirrorshades</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I think you mistook my point. My mention of science versus Coils was to highlight how science can empower the many as well as the individual, whereas Coils can only empower the individual. Its the so-called &quot;virtue of selfishness&quot; taken to its logical and horrifying conclusions. There's no balance to it. <br /> <br /> If the Carthians, taken to their utmost extreme are communists, and the Circle are anarchists, then the Ordo Dracul are Ann Rynn's devout followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:15:24-07:00","id":973168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=973152#post973152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think you mistook my point. My mention of science versus Coils was to highlight how science can empower the many as well as the individual, whereas Coils can only empower the individual. Its the so-called &quot;virtue of selfishness&quot; taken to its logical and horrifying conclusions. There's no balance to it.<br /> <br /> If the Carthians, taken to their utmost extreme are communists, and the Circle are anarchists, then the Ordo Dracul are Ann Rynn's devout followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely correct, I did misunderstand your intended point, most likely because bare text doesn't stress emphasis like a voice does and I most strongly noticed the part I responded to. With your reply I see how it also reads the way you are describing as well.<br /> <br /> It is interesting what you are doing. With the metaphorical paint brush, you are dipping into the pallet of political ideology to describe the 'feel' behind the Covenants. The result may not be a precise classical portrait, but it does make a vivid and valid impressionist picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=973081#post973081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unlike mundane sceince, which produces knowledge and technology that can spread and improve the lives of the many,</div> </div> </div> </div>I took this as strong praise for science since it is broached solely in positive terms. Your reply makes it clear that was just circumstantial phrasing and not a deliberate argument. Thus my counter was the applications of science was no less horrific than political or rebellious ideologies (ideologies just being memetic technologies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-20-2016, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:24:05-07:00","id":973171,"title":"","content":"I think of the Ordo Dracul as more Occult Transvampirism, with some influence from the scientific method then science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:53:33-07:00","id":973191,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> - *shrugs* The Ordo Dracul need something to be compared to, given the current discussion and comparisons of the Lance and Christianity. Science is the closest that I can come up with. I'm all ears for a better option, since &quot;science&quot; isn't even on the socio-political spectrum like the other covenants are.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> - Its admittedly hard to convey points over the text medium, especially for something that's really deserving of its own in-depth analysis and discussion; two sentences didn't do the entire subject any justice, and was admittedly misleading without the full context. Even now I'm doing a kind of rush job of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-20-2016, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:09:46-07:00","id":973202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=973191#post973191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> - *shrugs* The Ordo Dracul need something to be compared to, given the current discussion and comparisons of the Lance and Christianity. Science is the closest that I can come up with. I'm all ears for a better option, since &quot;science&quot; isn't even on the socio-political spectrum like the other covenants are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science (<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=science+definition&amp;ie=utf-8&amp;oe=utf-8\" target=\"_blank\">broad sense of the word</a>) is a valid term, since Ordo Dracul is all about a discovery methodology, which science is. Occult is the field being studied (you know, because they are supernatural beings instead of standard biological covered by medicine, and vampires/their abilities exist in the physical world even though they are occult beings), and Transvampirism is the goal, but an archaic scientific method of hypothesis - experimentation/research/studies - result is what they use to make discoveries.<br /> <br /> I see what you mean about the Ayn Rand, self-determinism being a major theme in their mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-20-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:57:01-07:00","id":977371,"title":"","content":"Science is more than just the scientific method. A large part of it is having a community dedicated to sharing research and verifying each others results. You can not have any real scientific endeavor without a community to facilitate discussion and verification. So yes, the Ordo Dracul is the definition of a society based on science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T03:49:11-07:00","id":977677,"title":"","content":"That's one aspect of them, and some are certainly exactly that, but I feel there is a strong element of spirituality in the Ordo Dracul still. First, basic research, while it can be aimed a certain way, is fairly unpredictable. The main goal is knowledge and you can't be certain what you're going to find. The goal of the Ordo Dracul isn't knowledge itself, it's transcendence. Knowledge, acquired though scientific methods, is just a means to an end. At the core, there is the idea, which you could call a belief or faith, that there is something beyond the vampiric condition that is attainable (be it gaining back one's humanity for the most idealistic of them, or just a vague notion of a better, more efficient predator, or some kind of demigod) and that the research has to be aimed that way.<br /> <br /> I'm waiting to see what secrets of the covenants say about the 2ed version, but in 1ed, you had lots of very philosophical practices like following the dragon's tail, which I saw as some sort of way of meditating on the impact your actions have on the world. Plus, you have the division into &quot;sworns&quot;, and the master/disciple dynamic that suggests an underlying philosophy. Honestly, the feeling I'm getting about the Ordo Dracul is more like Middle Age/Renaissance Alchemists looking for the philosopher's stone. From afar, it looks like it could be kind of scientific, but there's lots of weird ways of thinking, linking names to potential real effects, what a certain element looks like and what you think it could be used for depending on it... including the potential for the entire research to be a form of inner journey, with the elements, chemicals, and surgeries being nothing more than allegorical means of unlocking things within yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T03:53:19-07:00","id":977679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=977677#post977677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goal of the Ordo Dracul isn't knowledge itself, it's transcendence.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition yes, but in 2nd edition their purpose is to weaponize aspects of vampiric existence for the objective of overthrowing God.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:49:52-07:00","id":977839,"title":"","content":"Eh, that's true, but the point remains. Even more so.<br /> <br /> And well, I'd probably put that goal in the background in my games. It makes sense for the Lancea Sanctum to require faith in god since they're basically a religion/cult, but given what the Ordo does, I can't imagine they serve the rap that god made them vampires and he has to go down as a literal truth. For one, they would cut themselves from potential recruits that don't adhere to abrahamic religions which would be counterproductive, and second, it's such a distant and vague goal that very few people could stay focused on it for very long. The betterment of the vampiric condition is a concrete aspiration and so is the amassing of an individual\u2019s supernatural power, but the defeat of god ? Does that mean physically enter some heavenly realm and punching god in the face ? You could consider, from a christian standpoint, that any soul that does not accept god before dying a defeat.<br /> <br /> What I could see is a lot of dragons taking that goal as an allegorical statement with god representing anything they deem necessary to surpass or defeat. I mean, Ordo members get together to compare studies, show off their latest discoveries, discuss who's a danger to them, and talk about stuff they can do something about. It's not like they gather to form battle plans for how they're going to knock on heaven's door and give St Peter a wedgie when he answers the door. Some probably do, but that's what happens to vampires who don't go out enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:19:40-07:00","id":980622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=977679#post977679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In first edition yes, but in 2nd edition their purpose is to weaponize aspects of vampiric existence for the objective of overthrowing God.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're mistakenly conflating a philosophical opposition with an actual objective. The Ordo's shtick as far as God is concerned is an opposition to acting within the boundaries of a divine plan in order to reclaim agency over their condition, a metaphorical echo of how they claim agency over the Kindred Condition with the Coils.<br /> <br /> The anti-theism is probably interpreted in that fashion by most modern Ordo Dracul members, anyhow. Those who really get a kick out of being against God might take it more literally and try to oppose the Sanctified, but you never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:30:17-07:00","id":980629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=977839#post977839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, that's true, but the point remains. Even more so.<br /> <br /> And well, I'd probably put that goal in the background in my games. It makes sense for the Lancea Sanctum to require faith in god since they're basically a religion/cult, but given what the Ordo does, I can't imagine they serve the rap that god made them vampires and he has to go down as a literal truth. For one, they would cut themselves from potential recruits that don't adhere to abrahamic religions which would be counterproductive, and second, it's such a distant and vague goal that very few people could stay focused on it for very long. The betterment of the vampiric condition is a concrete aspiration and so is the amassing of an individual\u2019s supernatural power, but the defeat of god ? Does that mean physically enter some heavenly realm and punching god in the face ? You could consider, from a christian standpoint, that any soul that does not accept god before dying a defeat.<br /> <br /> What I could see is a lot of dragons taking that goal as an allegorical statement with god representing anything they deem necessary to surpass or defeat. I mean, Ordo members get together to compare studies, show off their latest discoveries, discuss who's a danger to them, and talk about stuff they can do something about. It's not like they gather to form battle plans for how they're going to knock on heaven's door and give St Peter a wedgie when he answers the door. Some probably do, but that's what happens to vampires who don't go out enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ohhh? And why wouldn't they do that? I mean, World of Darkness makes it blatantly clear that supernatural realms do, in fact, exist. You have the Supernal realms, one of which appears to be very reminiscent of Heaven. Then you have the world of dreams, which basically means you're walking around inside humanity's collective subconscious.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the Begotten have almost free reign to travel between any of these realms. They also seem to be happy to help out their &quot;relatives&quot; from time to time.<br /> <br /> It's not completely ridiculous to imagine that the Dragons would be preparing for a long term siege against Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T04:16:08-07:00","id":980697,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ok, that could be the plot of a massive campaign.<br /> <br /> Pretty hard, though. Not talking about the siege itself, but to arrive at that point. Beasts can be a good tool with theyr ability to open pathways, I suppose, but I think a mage would be better suited to actually tell what the realm they're going to is (Plus, it forces you to incorporate Beasts into your game and... I don't know. It's a conceptually interesting game and there are many many cool things to be done, but the eventual &quot;goal&quot; of the game, to become a supermonster that kicks dream ass seems really really underwhelming and ultimately pointless. Plus, it's a game where you can play a dragon but can't actually turn into a dragon. Boring.).<br /> <br /> So anyway, first, the dragons have to realize there exist other realms. That means tracking other supernatural and making them talk. Then, it depends what supernatural they get information from. If it's a changeling, they might conclude that god is some super true fae and start looking for ways to vandalize Arcadia. If it's a mage, they might hear about the Oneiros, Temenos, and Anima Mundi. Then, they have to decide, does god reside in the collective unconscious ? If so, they might track it down in the Temenos. Messing with the idea of god is a way to fight it. It would be a way to defeat god even for atheist/agnostic vampires, erasing it from humanity's collective consciousness. But if there has to be a being independent of human consciousness that is god, then it might be in the Anima Mundi, and good fucking luck mounting an expedition there. Of course, they could also meet demons and get told that god is a giant computer that has tendrils all over the world. At least, in that case, they might gain allies in their plan. Or they might be used as puppets by a couple of demons as a diversion and get slaughtered or worse while the unchained actually do something that damages the God Machine. Or what do I know, maybe they meet Prometheans and decide Pyros is god and they gotta take it down, but I got nothing there. Last case, maybe they decide all of those things are true and they might as well kick god's ass everywhere just to make sure.<br /> <br /> That sounds like a very, very fun campaign if the players aren't too afraid to die horribly. Honestly, one of the biggest problems with that is that once they start having enough info, they'll have to convince other vampires, you know, sane ones who'd like to keep existing a few more years, to join them in the great war against whatever they consider heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T05:26:20-07:00","id":980710,"title":"","content":"Well technically speaking, the &quot;dragon&quot; in this scenario refers to Lucifer. Dracula actually means &quot;son of the dragon&quot; or &quot;son of the devil&quot; because of the evil deeds he performed to earn that title.<br /> <br /> The Antichrist (another son of the devil) is said to be a <i>dragon</i> with 10 crowns atop 10 horns. They will conquer and rule the earth for 1,000 years before having the final battle against Christ.<br /> <br /> <br /> So for the Ordo Dracul, who actually claim to be founded by Dracula, it could be plausible.<br /> <br /> <br /> But all of this is their <b>long term</b> goal, and no member of the Order has been recorded to have completely succeeded in what they're trying to accomplish. Showing up on God's doorstep with an army of perfect vampires may not be possible for thousands of years, but it gives the Ordo Dracul something to focus on in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-03-2016, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:44:06-07:00","id":980767,"title":"","content":"Speaking to the original question, I really think it entirely comes down to nerd subculture having an antagonistic view of organized religion and Christianity that makes something Christian-adjacent like the Lancea unappealing. On a basic level, they look like Vampire Christians, and everybody hates Christians, so they don't want to be like that. On a deeper level, there's a lot of organizational principles of faith-based organizations that work on the communal level like churches that, for whatever reason, does not seem to jive with the mindset of a lot of Vampire players, which IMO is a shame, because I think the Sanctified offer the most fertile ground for exploring what being a vampire might do to religious beliefs, or how someone seeking answers might be driven into the church. My kingdom for someone who wants to play a character eager to participate in church politics for reform reasons in a given domain.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Circle has things which are aesthetically appealing to a lot of vampire players: They're blood witches, pagans, counter-culture types with a supposedly fierce focus on individualism and a way of personalizing the mythology of a character. Fondly remember the Humanity you lose and live it up as a goddess of the night kind of thing. Which is very viscerally appealing to a lot of vampire players, I think. The key, in my view, is that it's appealing to <i>players </i>but it's worth thinking about how initially appealing it might be to <i>characters</i>. The Circle is very nakedly different and unfamiliar and inhumane in a lot of ways that might be harder for a regular person turned neonate to appreciate, so I don't think they're as easy a sell ideologically. I can imagine that a lot of characters would be like Loki in the Chicago domain, in that they sit on the edge of the Circle, because their laissez faire way of doing things appeals, but they might be afraid of diving deeper.<br /> <br /> I think exploring how the Sanctified support young Kindred and the transformation from scared person afraid of the night into an Anointed dark creature of God could be really interesting if a player had an interest in pursuing it. Most people I've played with have not really, so I suppose it's a thing I aspire to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:18:03-07:00","id":980781,"title":"","content":"It's not so much a problem with them being Christians, but rather the fact that they are Old Testament style Christians. The kind of people who would organize flash mobs and nail you to a cross for speaking out against the Church. Don't forget their founder was a Roman centurion! Also, they believe that Satan is part of God's plan, and they seek to emulate him on earth in order to make his job (ruining our lives as a test of faith) easier to accomplish.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum is the vampire equivalent to the West Burrow Baptists. Sure, they're Christians, but they're complete ass holes about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone, on the other hand, is not a singular religion, but a vast collection of different religions. The 1st edition book includes a scenario in New Orleans, where the Circle practices Voodoo among the African community. It's more than just vampire freedom, it's religious freedom. You can be a follower of nearly any religion you want under the Circle of the Crone, and they seem to be much more lenient than the nigh impossible standards of fundamentalist Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-03-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:34:01-07:00","id":980785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980781#post980781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kind of people who would organize flash mobs and nail you to a cross for speaking out against the Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically inaccurate of Christianity. Flip the roles of persecution during the pre-Constantine Roman era, the Church started as brutalized martyrs who were horribly tortured and <a href=\"http://www.catholic.org/saints/saint.php?saint_id=366\" target=\"_blank\">robbed of their property</a>.<br /> <br /> The the game writers also demonstrate their knowledge of this this thus:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Testament of Longinus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1The triumphs and martyrdoms of the Dark Apostles, whom we call the Black <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Saints, are widely known among the Sanctified faithful, for their stories </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">are passed among us as an inspiration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">But it can only be a help to us to </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">see their tales in writing, and although I cannot imagine that a time will </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">come when the tales of the Black Saints and their miracles and their </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">final </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Deaths are not told to the enthralled assemblies of the Sanctified, it is up </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">to me </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">a </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">to write down the miracles of these first followers of Longinus.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">When Longinus left behind the Spear with the Monachus and walked into </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the world, he said:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cThe Blood of Christ gave sight to my blind eyes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">5</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201coctavian left my tongue and pulled my teeth, but I still commanded him </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">to abandon his idols.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">6</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cI have been buried and I have returned. I have been stricken down, and yet </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I have returned to my feet.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">7</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cIf these are not miracles, what are they?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">8</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cAnd yet, if they are miracles, why has God granted them to me, a vessel of sin?\u201d</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:46:31-07:00","id":980789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980767#post980767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think exploring how the Sanctified support young Kindred and the transformation from scared person afraid of the night into an Anointed dark creature of God could be really interesting if a player had an interest in pursuing it. Most people I've played with have not really, so I suppose it's a thing I aspire to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole, help new kindred come to term with their condition, and offer support like shelter or food, could be a very interesting program the Lancea does in conjunction with the Carthians.<br /> <br /> I'll go reread on elements of how the church did (and still do) community projects to help people and see how i could apply that to the All-Night Society. I think that would offer a good ''other side of the coin'' to the individualistic nature of the circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:20:13-07:00","id":980863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980789#post980789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the whole, help new kindred come to term with their condition, and offer support like shelter or food, could be a very interesting program the Lancea does in conjunction with the Carthians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go as far as suggesting that the Carthians are not a certainty for running such a program, they might be much more interested in giving resources to people that are inside the covenant already, while the Lancea is almost definitely going to do that, because they're proselytizing. Carthians might also not subscribe to the same political philosophies from place to place, while there is a near-certainty that the Sanctified will still be proselytizing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980789#post980789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll go reread on elements of how the church did (and still do) community projects to help people and see how i could apply that to the All-Night Society. I think that would offer a good ''other side of the coin'' to the individualistic nature of the circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is a good idea. I wouldn't literally ape modern church practices, but look at older ones and consider how it might diverge. If you've ever met a person who is affiliated with a church and really enthusiastic about it, ask them about what they like about it. A sense of belonging and clarity in an uncertain time might be a very attractive thing for regular people, even moreso for people made into Kindred.<br /> <br /> How do you navigate the ethics of feeding on people? Easy. You're Damned, you're supposed to do this. If you're feeling bad about it, maybe they deserve it because they failed your test, or maybe you'll defend the church against the city's attempt to foreclose in the coming months to make yourself feel better. Your humanity will wither, but it won't expire, because the Chapel &amp; Spear excoriates those who engage in the behaviors that lead to draugrdom. <br /> <br /> The kind of clarity that faith offers is much more attractive than people give it credit for, but I think that's because many of us put our faith in different things and are averse to the Christian symbol set of the Sanctified.<br /> <br /> I made a character who was an atheistic type in life but converted to the Sanctum in undeath. I'd love to play him some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:05:58-07:00","id":980895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980785#post980785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Historically inaccurate of Christianity. Flip the roles of persecution during the pre-Constantine Roman era, the Church started as brutalized martyrs who were horrible tortured and <a href=\"http://www.catholic.org/saints/saint.php?saint_id=366\" target=\"_blank\">robbed of their property</a>.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know they were treated badly, but they would eventually go onto become just as bad. The fall of Rome signaled the beginning of the Dark Ages, a time when Christianity rose to power and brutally enforced their religion on everyone around them. This is the kind of Christianity that the Lancea Sanctum embody.<br /> <br /> You think a few decades of indoctrination can traumatize a human worshiper? Try imagining a <i>few centuries</i> in a society that doesn't like to adapt itself to the modern era.<br /> <br /> The Invictus still expect everybody to recognize the class system, despite the fact that such a hierarchy has been extinct for centuries and from a modern day perspective, their esteemed heritage does not make them inherently superior to any common peasant.<br /> <br /> So how would somebody raised in a medieval Christian household react to seeing the outside world today?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:02:21-07:00","id":980925,"title":"","content":"Treated badly? Since inception, the very existence of Christianity was criminalized and they were tortured and murdered for their beliefs. To this day they are persecuted all over the world and forbidden to &quot;proselytize&quot; their beliefs even within their country of origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:21:10-07:00","id":980937,"title":"","content":"Not gonna argue the specifics, but Constantin made christianity legal in the Roman Empire after he personally converted. Then, the Edict of Thessalonica made it the official religion of the empire in 380 and outlawed the pagan religions as well as Greek inherited philosophies (the practitioners of which were then persecuted themselves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:40:47-07:00","id":980992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980781#post980781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much a problem with them being Christians, but rather the fact that they are Old Testament style Christians. The kind of people who would organize flash mobs and nail you to a cross for speaking out against the Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Romans nailed people to crosses to punish them. When Christians appropriated it as a symbol of their faith, it became pretty passe. I <i>loathe </i>engaging in this kind of comparison bullshit, but Christian suppression of non-Christian groups is not the sole province of Christianity, and religious persecution for differing faiths can be found in many other religions as well. My personal notion of it is that it's not an essential quality of any religion, but rather a toxic ideology which is most often recognized in religions, but YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980781#post980781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they believe that Satan is part of God's plan, and they seek to emulate him on earth in order to make his job (ruining our lives as a test of faith) easier to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a gross oversimplification of what the Sanctified believe, and not sufficiently nuanced to enhance the discussion. Satan is part of God's plan in conventional Christianity, the notion for the Sanctified is that they are Damned, condemned by God to be monsters, and that by being the wolves that stalk the lambs, they will drive people in the right direction, towards virtue and towards god. Their powers are thus meant to test us, to see if we can resist wicked temptation and monsters. An important bit that was there before but got emphasized in 2e is that they are also there to <i>protect the herd </i>from worse things and from bad stuff. Sometimes bad stuff might be a murderer, or a mage, or a demon. Other times bad stuff might be the kids who were fornicating and using drugs in the tabernacle. That capricious element is an important part of the alienation and discomfort one might feel among the Sanctified, but it is not their sole trait.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the Sanctified faith is about being a disciplined monster. That's not the same thing as a nice one, but by giving parameters for living ,advocating for austerity and humble purpose, the goal is to remove a lot of the temptations to be wasteful with their abilities that vampires have. Don't play with your food. Don't torment them just because. There's a purpose to it all, a plan.<br /> <br /> For many people, unsure of what to do with the eternity they now have in their hands, that's fairly compelling. A reason for being, a point to it all. A way of operating which takes your monstrous urges and supposes there's a constructive purpose to it all. You can be a hero, in your own way. A dark one, but ultimately a narrative of a person doing something theoretically valuable and constructive with their eternal damnation.<br /> <br /> Moreover, by enforcing things like austerity and strict hierarchy and discipline through prayer and learning, they offer a degree of control. Your humanity will inevitably wither as you participate in this inhuman instution, but its discipline promises a degree of stability. None of the other Covenants offer that kind of comfort. The Invictus does, half-heartedly, but we all understand that theirs is a more complicated balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980781#post980781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea Sanctum is the vampire equivalent to the West Burrow Baptists. Sure, they're Christians, but they're complete ass holes about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are assholes. The Invictus? Assholes. The Carthians? Holy <i>shit </i>are they assholes. The Ordo Dracul? Those assholes don't give a shit about anybody, and do horrible things purely for their own selfish advancement. The Circle of the Crone? Total, monstrous assholes, and they tell you to fuck off if you have a problem with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980781#post980781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Circle of the Crone, on the other hand, is not a singular religion, but a vast collection of different religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not identifying the consistent ideology of the Circle here, which <i>is </i>presented in the book. Their faiths might wear a thousand different little faces, but they're all connected by the same ideology, and it is not as nice and tolerant theology, it is a violent one. You and your beliefs have to survive both the domain and the Circle itself, which is not easy, and makes for a complicated relationship with neonates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980781#post980781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1st edition book includes a scenario in New Orleans, where the Circle practices Voodoo among the African community. It's more than just vampire freedom, it's religious freedom. You can be a follower of nearly any religion you want under the Circle of the Crone, and they seem to be much more lenient than the nigh impossible standards of fundamentalist Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baron Cimetiere does not espouse a philosophy of religious tolerance, if that's what you're suggesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:45:04-07:00","id":981031,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not going to argue that from a character stand point, the Lancea may be alluring. But the purpose of this thread was to get it from a player's stand point, if I'm not mistaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, the very concept of eternal punishment is something I am <i>very strongly</i> against. And an entire covenant that won't shut up about makes me very uncomfortable, to the point where I don't think I could slip into that role, even if it is just fantasy. Not only does the Lancea believe in hell, but they use the embrace as a means of punishing mortals. Which means they are consciously damning them to eternal punishment because Longinus accidentally drank some blood and spontaneously decided he had the right to pass judgement!<br /> <br /> <br /> Even if I joined the Lancea Sanctum (probably because I was coerced into it), I would pay them lip service at best, and bolt for a different covenant the first chance I got.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the religious tolerance thing, I was referring to the Circle as a whole allowing different faiths, not individual cults. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:04:08-07:00","id":981049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981031#post981031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm not going to argue that from a character stand point, the Lancea may be alluring. But the purpose of this thread was to get it from a player's stand point, if I'm not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they make for interesting roleplay? Because those compelling in-character reasons are compelling reasons to explore what kind of story they offer? Because they're way more nuanced and interesting than people give them credit for, because they think Christianity is all Westborough Baptist Church and that just because these guys wear funky crosses and believe in a vampire from the time of Christ who helped them figure out what to do besides be dicks for shitty reasons and become monsters?<br /> <br /> There's a lot there, but this gets into a weird discussion about player interest. If you as a player are too turned off by what smells faintly of Christianity, there's nothing much to be done to convince you, because that scent isn't going away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981031#post981031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, the very concept of eternal punishment is something I am <i>very strongly</i> against. And an entire covenant that won't shut up about makes me very uncomfortable, to the point where I don't think I could slip into that role, even if it is just fantasy. Not only does the Lancea believe in hell, but they use the embrace as a means of punishing mortals. Which means they are consciously damning them to eternal punishment because Longinus accidentally drank some blood and spontaneously decided he had the right to pass judgement!</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is a 'you' problem rather than a Sanctified problem? Because the practical notion of being Damned in the Sanctum is liberating. You're not a good person who can do bad things to make yourself bad, you're just bad now, so all that bad stuff you do? That doesn't make your lot any worse than it already is.<br /> <br /> The various descriptions of the Sanctified view on the Embrace is that it is heavily frowned upon but accepted as a part of the Kindred Condition. You're not really supposed to Embrace because the idea is that only God can judge someone so full of sin that they deserve eternal damnation, but realistically, Kindred will embrace, so they accommodate that. Some sects, like that of Solomon Birch, do not accommodate that and are very angry with the idea.<br /> <br /> So yes, they believe the Embrace is a punishment, but it's not one you're supposed to enact, or at the very least, don't enact it lightly. How do the other covenants feel? They don't give a hoot. That's kinda bad, because it means that there's nothing stopping people from Embracing others than some notion of the Masquerade and the consequences in a given domain. At least the Sanctified have parts of their dogma that say &quot;This is bad.&quot; You can read it in the Sanctum Covenant book (eh) or you could read it in the Testament of Longinus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981031#post981031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which means they are consciously damning them to eternal punishment because Longinus accidentally drank some blood and spontaneously decided he had the right to pass judgement!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Longinus in regular Christianity is an important figure because he pierced Christ's side with his lance, which, if you gather from the Crucifixion, was not the nicest thing to do. The Testament of Longinus lays it on even more thick, he wasn't in the wrong place at the wrong time, he was a sinful, indolent monster who slept with his mother, killed people, committed other grave crimes and sins, and was an all around scumbag. When he becomes Kindred, he is transformed from useless evil shithead to a dark creature of the night who protects and harries the flock to ensure that they are worthy of God's heaven. Redemption is a complicated, multi-layered thing, and while he is still Damned in this situation, Longinus has made something useful of his life, and found a way to have a purpose in God's plan. In that sense, he has redeemed himself, and that's a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981031#post981031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if I joined the Lancea Sanctum (probably because I was coerced into it), I would pay them lip service at best, and bolt for a different covenant the first chance I got.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. You'd be bolting for misinformed, wrong reasons, but hey, people do that sort of thing all the time. I'm just warning you, the Circle are like, very likely to be way less nice to you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981031#post981031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the religious tolerance thing, I was referring to the Circle as a whole allowing different faiths, not individual cults. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly the problem. There is no whole Circle, the Circle is made up of the cults. The cults are not tolerant, they don't espouse religious tolerance, they espouse a particular philosophy of the Kindred condition and if you don't fit that bill and survive the tribulation, you and your way of thinking greet the sun, and they celebrate by dancing on your ashes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-03-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:23:17-07:00","id":981067,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is a 'me' problem. Because I already pointed out that the point of the OP was to get a player's perspective of the covenant, not the character's perspective. And my player perspective is that I don't like the Lancea Sanctum for the reasons I described.<br /> <br /> In universe, you're right, the Lancea might offer relief to vampires who are looking for answers, or don't know the full scope of the Lancea's dogma. But I don't live in their universe. I live in ours, where the full scope of the Lancea is outlaid in a book. I know what they're about, and I don't like it.<br /> <br /> As for Longinus redeeming himself, that sounds like a bold face lie. You basically said that prior to his embrace, he was a shitty person. But after his embrace he became a better person by being a shitty person to other shitty people? It sounds like he was doing the exact same stuff, he just narrowed his focus on a vast margin of people as mandated by a religion he didn't even believe in prior to his embrace. Also, you can't be 'redeemed' and 'damned' at the same time.<br /> <br /> Those two are mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-03-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:51:26-07:00","id":981140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981067#post981067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Longinus redeeming himself, that sounds like a bold face lie. You basically said that prior to his embrace, he was a shitty person. But after his embrace he became a better person by being a shitty person to other shitty people? It sounds like he was doing the exact same stuff, he just narrowed his focus on a vast margin of people as mandated by a religion he didn't even believe in prior to his embrace. Also, you can't be 'redeemed' and 'damned' at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't suggesting that there is an objective metric for redemption, or that Longinus had met this hypothetical objective metric of redemption, rather that in the context of the faith of the Sanctified, his story told in the Testament of Longinus is that of an indolent and sinful person reborn as one of the Damned and given a newfound obligation to humanity as a predator of God. His redemption is not some abstract notion of going from bad to good, but the contextualized idea of transcending petty, indulgent evil for the kind of cruelty that is supposed to play a part in God's plan. He goes from being a useless bad person to a bad person with a purpose, which is a form of &quot;redemption&quot; within the context of vampirism. You hunted and drained that person not just to sate your hunger, but to punish him for his sinfulness.<br /> <br /> Basically, his journey from mortal sinner to immortal creature of God is supposed to suggest that the Sanctified too can put the evil in their heart towards a greater purpose as an instrument of God's plan, which lets the Sanctified tell themselves that all the things they would do anyway as vampires has a higher purpose. It's supposed to help you cope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:59:00-07:00","id":981145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980925#post980925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Treated badly? Since inception, the very existence of Christianity was criminalized and they were tortured and murdered for their beliefs. To this day they are persecuted all over the world and forbidden to &quot;proselytize&quot; their beliefs even within their country of origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about the criminalized, tortured and murdered Christianity that went on to sistematically criminalize, torture and murder people of all other religions as soon as it had power?<br /> <br /> Ah, ok...<br /> <br /> Israel is not the &quot;country of origin&quot; of Christianity. It is a state created by the British Authority, by way of U.S. pressure as &quot;reparations&quot; for the Jews. (or something like this, it is very complicated) <br /> <br /> A quick Wiki would let you know that everyone is allowed to proselytize in Israel, what is not allowed is to offer any material benefit for conversion. That is for all religions, not only Christianity.<br /> <br /> All of the western world is heavily christian. Very few places on the world are openly hostile to christians. Those places are pretty hostile to anyone in general.<br /> <br /> Stop victimizing yourself. It ain't pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:32:42-07:00","id":981161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980992#post980992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Romans nailed people to crosses to punish them. When Christians appropriated it as a symbol of their faith, it became pretty passe. I <i>loathe </i>engaging in this kind of comparison bullshit, but Christian suppression of non-Christian groups is not the sole province of Christianity, and religious persecution for differing faiths can be found in many other religions as well. My personal notion of it is that it's not an essential quality of any religion, but rather a toxic ideology which is most often recognized in religions, but YMMV.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody ever claimed anything resembling the idea that persecution of other faiths is the sole province of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Christianity is, however, the dominant faith of the Western world, and thus players who have been religiously persecuted and discriminated against are most likely to have had it been at the hands of Christianity, which is kind of the crux of the answer to the thread's topic. It doesn't matter if other faiths also persecute, because this fact is irrelevant to the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can see why a group of people who believe it's their God-given reason for existence to persecute and judge others (regardless of faith, at least) might be uncomfortable for these people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:52:37-07:00","id":981176,"title":"","content":"Of course! I'm not arguing that it shouldn't make you uncomfortable, just that to think of it as something that makes the Lancea et Sanctum demonstrably worse than their counterparts seems to be a really myopic perspective. Like, the other Covenants are <i>awful </i>and the Lancea et Sanctum isn't like, <i>more </i>awful because we're <i>less </i>desensitized to the trappings of their inhumane practice. Particularly, there's a way that the Circle is romanticized in comparison that feels really horrifying, especially when you consider how they prey on and exploit spaces which are often occupied by marginalized groups.<br /> <br /> Like, all the covenants to one degree or another believe that their existence is justified by a capacity to enact power over others through the Kindred condition. Carthians see mortals as the means of production, not the proletariat. The Invictus embody a vicious social darwinism that could make a free market die-hard blanche. The Ordo Dracul is happy to murder as many people as they care as long as it advances their personal notion of apotheosis and the Circle of the Crone is going to bathe in mortal blood because they think they are the gods and goddesses of the night, and mortals are just food, playthings and sacrificial lambs.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if your point is that some people just can't engage with the concept because it hits too close to home, that's fair. Can't really do much to change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-03-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:43:50-07:00","id":982823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=981145#post981145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Israel is not the &quot;country of origin&quot; of Christianity. It is a state created by the British Authority, by way of U.S. pressure as &quot;reparations&quot; for the Jews. (or something like this, it is very complicated)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In case you missed it, it was also a kingdom (populated and ran by Jews) which existed long before the British Mandate, or the Roman occupation as well for that matter.<br /> <br /> Revisionist attempts at rewriting history are even more ugly than self victimization.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to the topic, the Circle is more popular than the Lancea Sanctum simply as a matter of rebellion. Being anti-Christian in today's world is now hip and cool. And so rejecting anything that remotely resembles any facet of Christianity become cool and popular in a game that contains any whiff of it.<br /> <br /> One would imagine that in the near future, the Malkavian bloodline will become the popular group for the cool kids who want to reject things like objective standards or reality.<br /> <br /> The Vampire card game even went so far as to change its name after a particular event. Popularity among clans, bloodlines, and covenants will sway and move with the zeitgeist of the players. What is popular today, will be reviled tomorrow, and will be cool again one day. It all revolves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:43:05-07:00","id":982863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In case you missed it, it was also a kingdom (populated and ran by Jews) which existed long before the British Mandate, or the Roman occupation as well for that matter. </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing the point. It's wildy anachronistic to talk of Christianity having a country of origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:54:21-07:00","id":982869,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> has the right of what the LeS are about and what they believe. They're also right that they're not any better or worse than the other Covenants. All of the Covenants are supposed to provide answers to the question, &quot;what do I do now that I'm a monster?&quot;, and all of those answers are supposed to look reasonable and appealing from the perspective of a monster, but twisted and wrong from the perspective of a normal person. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, you absolutely should, from a player perspective, be made uncomfortable by the LeS's philosophy, that's working as intended. Vampire is supposed to be about playing anti-aspirational characters, their outlooks are supposed to make us uncomfortable. It makes many people more uncomfortable than the Circle of the Crone does for a variety of reasons, including being uncomfortable with its Christian trappings, being uncomfortable with its misapplication of Christian ideals, etc. What it comes down to a lot of the time is simply that Christianity has more baggage for most of us than Paganism does. But make no mistake, the Circle is every bit as monstrous as the Sanctum. As are the Carthians, the Invictus, and the Dragons. But everyone has biases and we can't prevent those biases from coloring our interpretation of information, and since Christianity weighs heavy in many of our lives, the Sanctum ends up getting less sympathy from Christians and non-Christians alike than other Covenants. It is what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:56:27-07:00","id":982870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=982863#post982863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's wildy anachronistic to talk of Christianity having a country of origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anachronistic, but accurate.<br /> <br /> An event occurred. An origin. That origin occurred in a place. Most places, that actually exist on our world, occur in a... wait for it.....waaaaiiiiiit for it....<br /> <br /> Country.<br /> <br /> Hairsplitters may quibble over the definition of that place, whether it is a country, province, territory, empire, satrapy, or any other term. But the current colloquial in common use is Country.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes. It may be considered old fashioned, but countries do still exist. Just as they did then. And likely will tomorrow, special snowflakes notwithstanding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:32:20-07:00","id":982895,"title":"","content":"Of course the thing that got left by the wayside is that people are not particularly prohibited from doing Christian stuff in Israel, which was the more important/relevant of the two parts of that statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:17:50-07:00","id":982925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An event occurred. An origin. That origin occurred in a place. Most places, that actually exist on our world, occur in a... wait for it.....waaaaiiiiiit for it....<br /> <br /> Country. </div> </div> </div>Places don't really occur. Events that happen in places occur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=982870#post982870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hairsplitters may quibble over the definition of that place, whether it is a country, province, territory, empire, satrapy, or any other term. But the current colloquial in common use is Country.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not hairsplinting. It's basic historical terminology. 'Country' refers to a modern nation-state structure, not the geography itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the current colloquial in common use is Country. </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. No one refers to the Roman Empire or the province of Judea as a country.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just as they did then. </div> </div> </div>No they didn't. The idea of a defined territory which is the basic element of a modern country wasn't really something that the Roman world had a clear idea of; mainly because that wasn't how power structures of the time functioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:27:10-07:00","id":982960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=982925#post982925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No it isn't. No one refers to the Roman Empire or the province of Judea as a country.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it was an empire that spanned the length of Europe and maybe further beyond that (I'm not sure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T18:04:58-07:00","id":983050,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the use of country (in the modern sense) comes along with the modern nation state. The Roman empire was various city states and subordinate territories/states all controlled by Rome (also a city state). People make the mistake of thinking of Roman like it was a modern nation state but that concept didn't exist in antiquity. Theres a reason that Nationalism is a rather modern idea (18 century with the modern nation state really only being formed after the French revolution, in Europe at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 10-06-2016, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:34:03-07:00","id":983567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=982823#post982823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In case you missed it, it was also a kingdom (populated and ran by Jews) which existed long before the British Mandate, or the Roman occupation as well for that matter.<br /> <br /> Revisionist attempts at rewriting history are even more ugly than self victimization.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> In case you missed it, there where people there before the Jews who got to rule it by slaughtering the previous inhabitants in &quot;holy&quot; war, it is right there in both Books, you can read about it. My stomach turns everytime I hear a little kid sing about the walls of Jericho tumbling down. And then other people came and took it from them. And then somebody else did the same to those guys. And on, and on, and on...<br /> <br /> That area has traded hands so many times that no one has any true right to it. It is held through strength of arms and, nowadays, a bit through modern diplomacy and globalization.<br /> <br /> Can you please show where I am being revisionist? Or is this your attempt at sophism?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=982823#post982823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the topic, the Circle is more popular than the Lancea Sanctum simply as a matter of rebellion. Being anti-Christian in today's world is now hip and cool. And so rejecting anything that remotely resembles any facet of Christianity become cool and popular in a game that contains any whiff of it.<br /> <br /> One would imagine that in the near future, the Malkavian bloodline will become the popular group for the cool kids who want to reject things like objective standards or reality.<br /> <br /> The Vampire card game even went so far as to change its name after a particular event. Popularity among clans, bloodlines, and covenants will sway and move with the zeitgeist of the players. What is popular today, will be reviled tomorrow, and will be cool again one day. It all revolves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Anti-christian being popular is very 80s and 90s. Get with the times, cool thing nowadays is to say it doesn\u00b4t matter.<br /> <br /> People that dislike the Spear because it is a twisted view of Christianity are just biased. <br /> <br /> People readily accept the Circle because of their negative bias towards Paganism. They see monsters being pagans as the natural states of monsters and pagans. So they like them for &quot;keeping ti real&quot;. The twisted outlook presented on the book matches their inner bias. Comfort and like.<br /> <br /> They see what are supposed to be the &quot;Christians&quot; and think they should be striving for something &quot;Good&quot;. Instead they are presented with a similarly twisted view of things, but now it does not match their preconceptions. It goes against their positive bias. Discomfort and dislike.<br /> <br /> People tend to cheer for this that they like and are comfortable with. All Covenants are tainted, shattered mirror reflections of human ideas/institutions. To accept one and not the other for what they are shows lazyness of thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=982895#post982895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the thing that got left by the wayside is that people are not particularly prohibited from doing Christian stuff in Israel, which was the more important/relevant of the two parts of that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is usually the case with people who want to &quot;win&quot; instead of engaging. Then they split hairs while complaining that others are hairsplitting. To note;<br /> <br /> Pointer: &quot;Christianity is persecuted all over the world (mindboggle)! It can\u00b4t even spread it\u00b4s Gospel in it\u00b4s country of origin!&quot;<br /> <br /> Counterpointer: &quot;&quot;No its is not. It is actually the majority religion in all western civilization. The places that are hostile to Christianity are generally shit holes and hostile to everyone. Besides the State of Israel is not the country of origin of Christianity, and you are allowed to spread it\u00b4s Gospel there. The thing it is not allowed to do is to promise them cars, houses and money for converting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hairsplitter: &quot;You`re splitting hairs! You\u00b4re so bad! So let me split those hairs even further and bicker about what a country is or isn\u00b4t and ignore the argument that Christian Persecution is a ridiculous fantasy unless you\u00b4re living North Korea (or select areas of Africa and the Middle-East).&quot;<br /> <br /> Counterpointer: Head ---&gt; Desk.<br /> <br /> Conclusion:<br /> <br /> &quot;Splitting hairs&quot; while addressing the points made. = Good.<br /> <br /> &quot;Splitting hairs&quot; while complaining about others splitting hairs and not addressing the point at all. = Bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T02:21:34-07:00","id":984322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=980785#post980785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Historically inaccurate of Christianity. Flip the roles of persecution during the pre-Constantine Roman era, the Church started as brutalized martyrs who were horribly tortured and <a href=\"http://www.catholic.org/saints/saint.php?saint_id=366\" target=\"_blank\">robbed of their property</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...I shouldn't do this. I really shouldn't. I should just walk away... oh, I can't. I apologise in advance to everyone for the vehemence of my rant.<br /> <br /> You do know that Christianity's history of martyrdom is predominantly a falsehood, right? The vast majority of stories about martyrs and persecution are either outright fiction, drastically manipulated away from the truth to support the myth, or so dubious that we can't figure out which they are. The comparatively tiny percentage of martyrs that actually existed have been drastically expanded in numbers and prominence.<br /> <br /> For the 300 years between the purported death of Jesus Christ and Emperor Constantine making Christianity the dominant religion of the Roman Empire, they were persecuted for perhaps 10-12 years, and even then, those years weren't concurrent and enforcement of the official persecution was very haphazard; some regions, usually those that had seen considerable Jewish uprisings before, were strict as the stories claim, but most did everything they could to <b>avoid</b> having to execute Christians.<br /> <br /> In fact, the early Christians were so eager to martyr themselves and thusly win a guaranteed place in Heaven, that they would openly confront Roman officials and beg to be put to death. A plea that the officials would do everything in their power to not grant, up to and including simply telling the Christians to bugger off and refusing to pay any attention to them.<br /> <br /> Before you take the obvious route and point to the very site linked in my quote, keep in mind that this is the same organization I am telling you repeatedly committed fraud to promote their own agenda. &quot;Lying for Jesus&quot;, they called it. For example, the infamous passage in Tactitus has been proven the result of forgerous additions to the original texts by an 11th century monk Actual historical evidence points very contrary.<br /> <br /> For example, in 112 AD, Pliny the Younger sent a letter to Emperor Trajan asking how he should deal with Christians. He was told, in response, not to seek them out, not to believe anonymous accusations, and to give them every opportunity to agree to be good Romans, at which point they should be released unharmed.<br /> <br /> Even when Christians were legally punished, the cause was practical and secular, not religious. Christians were seen by the Romans as alarmingly superstitious, rumored to engage in cannibalism and incestuous, and more practically being at best disrespectful and at worst outright seditious; the Romans took a dim view to doomsayers actively calling for the downfall of their Empire, and even Pliny's famous letter mostly dwells on his fears that the Christian cults are hotbeds of anti-Roman sedition. That's generally when the Christians came to be actively pushed; when their refusal to respect the emperor and thus show solidarity with the empire coincided with strong external strife.<br /> <br /> The actual truth of Christianity is that, for the vast majority of three hundred years, they were either completely ignored or granted special privileges. Emperor Trajan very much set the mold for his fellow emperors in that he did everything he could to grant them special favors and reasons to ignore them - even Emperor Hadrian, who absolutely hated all Judaic sects after the three years war he spent fighting against fanatical Jewish uprisings, was content to live and let live towards Jews, Christians and all the other Abrahamic sects of the day.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for whether or not knowledge of this colors players against the Sanctum and towards the Circle, I don't know. You can point to just about any Catholic or Protestant preacher on the net and you can be sure they'll disavow these facts, asserting it's simply anti-Christian prejudice and persecution, so I hardly expect them to be known amongst most Requiem players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:42:57-07:00","id":984489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=984322#post984322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I shouldn't do this. I really shouldn't. I should just walk away... oh, I can't. I apologise in advance to everyone for the vehemence of my rant.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't have to apologize for giving others a proper education. Thumbs up to you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:16:32-07:00","id":984512,"title":"","content":"We getting all historically nerdy in here. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:40:13-07:00","id":984972,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5487\" data-vbnamecard=\"5487\">VoidDrifter</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/politics/war/isis.asp\" target=\"_blank\">I am certain &quot;historic&quot; accuracy is as easily contested and debated as modern news, if not more so</a>. Witness accounts vary, and slinging of accusation of falsifying testimony (accurately AND inaccurately) is as old as people falsifying testimony, which has been happening since the fall of man. History is a thing in constant revision based on current world views and not necessarily new found facts, and I think that is a shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-10-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:38:08-07:00","id":985076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=984972#post984972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5487\" data-vbnamecard=\"5487\">VoidDrifter</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/politics/war/isis.asp\" target=\"_blank\">I am certain &quot;historic&quot; accuracy is as easily contested and debated as modern news, if not more so</a>. Witness accounts vary, and slinging of accusation of falsifying testimony (accurately AND inaccurately) is as old as people falsifying testimony, which has been happening since the fall of man. History is a thing in constant revision based on current world views and not necessarily new found facts, and I think that is a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True, and it's nearly always falsified to support the party telling it. <br /> <br /> Best course of action is to find an account written by a neutral party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:47:48-07:00","id":985083,"title":"","content":"Hard to do when all the neutral parties are dead.<br /> <br /> And by the way, Constantine didn't make Christianity the default religion of the empire; that was his successor in 367 AD. Constantine is the one who called the early church fathers together in 325 AD and forced them to form the Council of Nicaea so that he could justify making intolerance <i>against</i> Christianity illegal. He forced them to become a single religion instead of a disparate group of mystery cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:25:17-07:00","id":985118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985076#post985076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, and it's nearly always falsified to support the party telling it.<br /> <br /> Best course of action is to find an account written by a neutral party.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's nearly always falsified to support the party telling it.&quot; This is inaccurate and I'll demonstrate why, it benefits you to testify you are not a murderer, thereby the logic used in the proceeding argument you'd &quot;nearly always&quot; (interesting concept, by the way) be lying about not being a murderer. This does not align with the reality of most people claiming not to be a murderer thus the logic used is fallacious. (The False Belief being that a party testifying having a vested stake in a positive outcome requires that the truth cannot be aligned with the positive outcome, and thus they <i>MUST </i>be nearly always lying.)<br /> <br /> The best coarse of action is to use discernment to determine the most credible witnesses, who may or may not have interests in the matter because neutrality does not predicate a person has any insight or expertise, merely they lack motivation for perjury. Credibility is a confluence of factors, because reality is complex, and simplistic solutions tend to fail in dealing with complexity with finesse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-10-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:50:21-07:00","id":985127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985118#post985118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;It's nearly always falsified to support the party telling it.&quot; This is inaccurate and I'll demonstrate why, it benefits you to testify you are not a murderer, thereby the logic used in the proceeding argument you'd &quot;nearly always&quot; (interesting concept, by the way) be lying about not being a murderer. This does not align with the reality of most people claiming not to be a murderer thus the logic used is fallacious. (The False Belief being that a party testifying having a vested stake in a positive outcome requires that the truth cannot be aligned with the positive outcome, and thus they <i>MUST </i>be nearly always lying.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You lost me about half way through the second line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm so confused!<br /> <br /> I was saying the one telling the story will usually try to embellish the details in order to make themselves seem like the wounded party. The best thing to do is to find somebody who witnessed the events, but doesn't have strong ties to either side and hear what they have to say about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-10-2016, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:03:48-07:00","id":985134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985127#post985127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You lost me about half way through the second line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm so confused!<br /> <br /> I was saying the one telling the story will usually try to embellish the details in order to make themselves seem like the wounded party. The best thing to do is to find somebody who witnessed the events, but doesn't have strong ties to either side and hear what they have to say about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you are saying, and while it may be true in some cases it certainly isn't necessarily true, and thus fallacious (based on false belief that the principle is universally &lt;or &quot;nearly always&quot;, as you would say&gt;) .<br /> <br /> The best coarse of action is to use discernment to determine the most credible witnesses, who may or may not have interests in the matter because neutrality does not predicate a person has any insight or expertise, merely they lack motivation for perjury. Credibility is a confluence of factors, because reality is complex, and simplistic solutions tend to fail in dealing with complexity with finesse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-11-2016, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:16:34-07:00","id":985140,"title":"","content":"What is happening is that little by little (at a very slow pace, unfortunately) people are starting to question and demand evidence in order to believe things they are told.<br /> <br /> It is not enough to be told by a priest or for it to be written in a book. Even more so by a book that is a collection of (many times delirious) anecdotes by mostly unverified writers with a dog on the race. And then all this stuff got edited by people trying to institutionalize faith. Color me unimpressed if the facts are somewhat different than what is written.<br /> <br /> It is not sad that nowadays people question and scrutinize. It is one of the brightest happenings of the new times. We are at the first minutes of the dawn of reason.Many (most) people still need to open their eyes. Hopefully no calamity will reverse this.<br /> <br /> Everything will change, including history and religion. And that is a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:23:29-07:00","id":985182,"title":"","content":"Err, I believe the dawn of reason was back in the age of enlightenment. (arguably ancient greece). Lets not get too hyperbolic here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:34:28-07:00","id":985319,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that the catholic Church losing ground was more a result of people being fed up with it having so much political power than the people suddenly gaining incredible insight. Most big religious movements are just as much about politics and power as they are about spirituality. Religion, no matter how well nice looking, always creates power dynamics. Someone holds the truth and has the authority to distribute it to other people. Over time, that dynamic can become oppressive, and when someone starts speaking or acting against that oppression, they'll also want to subvert its spiritual component. You can fight against a corrupt church, but if people still recognize that the pope is infallible, you're the bad guy. This is a great tool for the powers, whatever they are. The French monarchy claimed it was chosen by god, so even it the king was being a giant douchebag, if that's god's will, you just have to shut up.<br /> <br /> Thing is nobody thinks they're the bad guy, so they'll have to find a way to keep opposing the oppressive power that makes sense. And I'm not saying that all revolutions are &quot;fake&quot; and that the spiritual, philosophical or political arguments are always just a pretext for a coup. These things are organic, they take time, and the people who do it are, I think, mostly honest about it. The protestants cut themselves from the Catholic church, but I'm pretty sure a lot of them really felt like it was corrupt and that not indulging in the cult of saints and decorating churches with gold would make them closer to god. The Russian Revolution probably targeted the Orthodox Church because it was backing up the Tsar, but socialism is a very serious current of thought, not just a way for Lenin to become the big boss.<br /> <br /> I'm missing a LOT of details here, but the point is that people don't just wise up suddenly, they don't revolt because they had an epiphany and now they know the truth. They stand up against an oppressive system that can take various shapes and usually get behind a certain way of thinking that contrasts that shape. In the case of the Catholic Church, there's little point in talking about it's spiritual elements without taking into account the power dynamics it generates, and vice-versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T05:35:51-07:00","id":985361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985319#post985319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the impression that the catholic Church losing ground was more a result of people being fed up with it having so much political power than the people suddenly gaining incredible insight. Most big religious movements are just as much about politics and power as they are about spirituality. Religion, no matter how well nice looking, always creates power dynamics. Someone holds the truth and has the authority to distribute it to other people. Over time, that dynamic can become oppressive, and when someone starts speaking or acting against that oppression, they'll also want to subvert its spiritual component. You can fight against a corrupt church, but if people still recognize that the pope is infallible, you're the bad guy. This is a great tool for the powers, whatever they are. The French monarchy claimed it was chosen by god, so even it the king was being a giant douchebag, if that's god's will, you just have to shut up.<br /> <br /> Thing is nobody thinks they're the bad guy, so they'll have to find a way to keep opposing the oppressive power that makes sense. And I'm not saying that all revolutions are &quot;fake&quot; and that the spiritual, philosophical or political arguments are always just a pretext for a coup. These things are organic, they take time, and the people who do it are, I think, mostly honest about it. The protestants cut themselves from the Catholic church, but I'm pretty sure a lot of them really felt like it was corrupt and that not indulging in the cult of saints and decorating churches with gold would make them closer to god. The Russian Revolution probably targeted the Orthodox Church because it was backing up the Tsar, but socialism is a very serious current of thought, not just a way for Lenin to become the big boss.<br /> <br /> I'm missing a LOT of details here, but the point is that people don't just wise up suddenly, they don't revolt because they had an epiphany and now they know the truth. They stand up against an oppressive system that can take various shapes and usually get behind a certain way of thinking that contrasts that shape. In the case of the Catholic Church, there's little point in talking about it's spiritual elements without taking into account the power dynamics it generates, and vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This <b>so</b> hard. Divested of political power, a religion is just a spiritual and moral framework built around a metaphysical belief structure. Its adherents can be good or bad, but the religion itself very rarely is (please refrain from providing examples to the contrary as it is obviously a very subjective topic). The Catholic Church promoted literacy during the reign of Charlemagne, funded natural philosophers throughout the Middle Ages and Renaissance, and provided humanitarian aid to countless peoples across history regardless of the predominant sentiment towards those people. It also promoted witch hunts and crusades and graft among its clergy. Catholicism isn't to &quot;blame&quot; for those things, nor is it &quot;responsible&quot; for the former things. It's an idea, it can't take agency for anything. People are the ones who take the trappings of a religion and use them for selfish purposes, and when that religion is also the state it becomes easier to get away with. This leads, as Brachen said, to resistance against oppression, which naturally takes a contrasting view to what it perceives as the enemy in order to better define itself (we like doing this as humans, we're hardwired to do it, in fact).<br /> <br /> Every time in history that the Church and the State have allied, it's ended badly for both. It was true for Egypt (like, four times), China, Japan, and everywhere else the Divine Right of Kings or the Celestial Mandate of Heaven or whatever was present. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:36:47-07:00","id":985438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985319#post985319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of the Catholic Church, there's little point in talking about it's spiritual elements without taking into account the power dynamics it generates, and vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frank Herbert, Dune</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/quotes/43262-when-religion-and-politics-travel-in-the-same-cart-the\" target=\"_blank\">\u201cWhen religion and politics travel in the same cart, the riders believe nothing can stand in their way. Their movements become headlong - faster and faster and faster. They put aside all thoughts of obstacles and forget the precipice does not show itself to the man in a blind rush until it's too late.\u201d</a></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7104\" data-vbnamecard=\"7104\">S. Brechen</a> Also I really liked your post; it was insightful.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Separation of church and state (which isn't a phrase in the founding documents but in a letter written by Thomas Jefferson to the Church explaining the intent of the first Amendment, check it out because it is neat to be culturally literate.) in addition to its other benefits like allowing diversity of faith, and lack of governmental persecution, also prevents the feedback loop of power-hungry political corruption infecting the church which then sets moral standards to excuse the corruption because it is part of the corruption, which make worse and worse things permissible. Of course a completely morally permissive society has the same problem but on an even broader scale, not just the top down.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">[^Disclaimer: Spoiler Contains Political Ideology]</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-11-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:17:13-07:00","id":985458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985182#post985182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err, I believe the dawn of reason was back in the age of enlightenment. (arguably ancient greece). Lets not get too hyperbolic here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u00b4t say it started now. I said we\u00b4re still living it. The world at large is still mired in the miasma of ignorance.<br /> <br /> Until a few years a ago I thought we were much further into a time where reason is the main guide for people\u00b4s minds. Until a conversation I had in my workplace, in the IT department (I\u00b4m a SAP consultant).<br /> <br /> I was talking to a colleague around lunchtime and the conversation somehow drifted into evolution. That is when I made a joke about Adam and Eve. And to my surprise that is what he believed.<br /> <br /> Dumbfounded, I asked, if that is actually what he believed, like actually, not some intelligent design thing of why it happened, but the actual story of out of mud and out of a rib. And he said &quot;Yah, the actual story&quot;. Then a another colleague overheard the conversation and &quot;came out&quot; as a cretionist. Then another. And another.<br /> <br /> Stupefied I went asking all my other colleagues, hoping for a light in the end of the tunnel. Out of 11 people I asked only one, timidly, accepted the facts of evolution.<br /> <br /> These were all people with Bachelors or Masters degrees in STEM or Business. Business process experts, DBAs, developers, engineers and admnistrators.<br /> <br /> Then you look at the all the shit in the world, zoom out in your time perspective and feel comforted that, thankfully, it is still the first minutes after dawn. It will get much brighter.<br /> <br /> It is common for people of a particular age to feel they live in a special era. But we actually do.<br /> <br /> Science is screaming at us in an ever increasing volume. Even the people that are deaf to it can feel the reverberating waves. They can\u00b4t just outright ignore it anymore. They squirm and twist trying to avoid it.<br /> <br /> I hope to live to see the day that it is so loud and clear that only the completely ignorant and irascible will attempt to misrepresent or silence it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:24:57-07:00","id":985679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985458#post985458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn\u00b4t say it started now. I said we\u00b4re still living it. The world at large is still mired in the miasma of ignorance.<br /> <br /> Until a few years a ago I thought we were much further into a time where reason is the main guide for people\u00b4s minds. Until a conversation I had in my workplace, in the IT department (I\u00b4m a SAP consultant).<br /> <br /> I was talking to a colleague around lunchtime and the conversation somehow drifted into evolution. That is when I made a joke about Adam and Eve. And to my surprise that is what he believed.<br /> <br /> Dumbfounded, I asked, if that is actually what he believed, like actually, not some intelligent design thing of why it happened, but the actual story of out of mud and out of a rib. And he said &amp;quot;Yah, the actual story&amp;quot;. Then a another colleague overheard the conversation and &amp;quot;came out&amp;quot; as a cretionist. Then another. And another.<br /> <br /> Stupefied I went asking all my other colleagues, hoping for a light in the end of the tunnel. Out of 11 people I asked only one, timidly, accepted the facts of evolution.<br /> <br /> These were all people with Bachelors or Masters degrees in STEM or Business. Business process experts, DBAs, developers, engineers and admnistrators.<br /> <br /> Then you look at the all the shit in the world, zoom out in your time perspective and feel comforted that, thankfully, it is still the first minutes after dawn. It will get much brighter.<br /> <br /> It is common for people of a particular age to feel they live in a special era. But we actually do.<br /> <br /> Science is screaming at us in an ever increasing volume. Even the people that are deaf to it can feel the reverberating waves. They can\u00b4t just outright ignore it anymore. They squirm and twist trying to avoid it.<br /> <br /> I hope to live to see the day that it is so loud and clear that only the completely ignorant and irascible will attempt to misrepresent or silence it.</div> </div> </div> </div> If it make you feel better I believe evolution, leaning towards puncuated equalibrium.<br /> <br /> I'm still a spiritual neo pagan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:13:14-07:00","id":985708,"title":"","content":"I think they're both pretty damn monstrous (and I also think that was intentional).<br /> <br /> But, given the prominence of Christianity, and particularly the Catholic Church, for the past few centuries, there's more baggage associated with their indiscretions. And more people are likely to have dealt with overbearing or fanatical Christianity than from fanatical paganism. So the Circle might seem more sympathetic by default. Everyone loves an underdog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:32:48-07:00","id":985915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=985679#post985679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it make you feel better I believe evolution, leaning towards puncuated equalibrium.<br /> <br /> I'm still a spiritual neo pagan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I myself believe in a syncretic mess of brazilianized Yoruba, Kardecist Spiritism, a sprinkle of Yoga and whatever scientific flavored musing my uneducated mind comes up with and I feel makes sense. I've been tormented by spirits, heard, seen and felt some very scary shit (most of it stopped after Candombl\u00e9/Umbanda rituals). I've had life changing ecstatic mystical experiences by partaking in Ayahuasca (after which all of my spiritual experiences are positive). I've benefited from watching a Louise Hay documentary, doing a self forgiveness mental exercise then going to sleep to have the most liberating dream of my life.<br /> <br /> I cried watching The Passion of the Christ. I respect the story and believe really great things came and could still come from it's lessons. Jesus is great and awesome.<br /> <br /> There is a very good Gandhi quote on this one. It is confrontational, so I won't post it here but is easily found with a little interest.<br /> <br /> So I'm not some anti-septic metallic atheist. I'm a monogamous married man, father of two and a corporate lackey who is also on a crazy pantheist spiritual adventure that I hope will last until death, and then some.<br /> <br /> I accept that someone may come and say &quot;Hey maybe you're just delusional&quot;. No shit. Theres obviously a chance that thats the case. If someone affirms that and diagnoses me though, I'll tell them to stop wasting time one me and go revolutionize mental health care. The world needs it.<br /> <br /> Things is, I don't want any of that taught in schools or made into the Law of any land. And I couldn't care less if anyone else believes in me or shares my beliefs (except this would make ritual celebrations very boring without the people and music. So make that as long as few gifted musicians share my beliefs I couldn't care less).<br /> <br /> I can't sit here and watch my children and delight in how powerful genetics are and make use of modern medicine and at the same time deny the very structural facts that made these understandings and achievements possible. I can't be amazed at the universe and be a flat earther nut. I can't look at fossils and appreciate geology and say the Earth is 6000 years old (or whatever ridiculous number people claim it to be). I can't say I appreciate history while I don't entertain arguments on plausibility, verifiability and probability of certain facts just because they're dear to the things I believe in.<br /> <br /> And I'm baffled that people do just that. With age I just learned to take it in stride, but it is still a head---&gt;desk moment to be exposed to this. I kept a good working relationship with all my colleagues. And the two people that became my personal friends were in the creationist camp. It is not about disliking or putting down christians, and it is sad and weak when people try to make it seem that way.<br /> <br /> I believe in God, though my God is not the god of St. Augustine but the One of Giordano Bruno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T21:03:29-07:00","id":985930,"title":"","content":"I believe the desire to root Acolyte over Sanctified stems most from the default state of VtR being an Invictus city with strong ties to the Sanctified. This lends the underdog motif to the remaining three Covenants, which makes them far easier to sympathize with than those in power. <br /> <br /> If say....a Circle of the Crone controlled city was going around hunting down Lancea et Sanctum Coteries, like in that one story from the Strix Chronicle Anthology, along with any other threats to the faith then it would be much easier to sympathize with the Sanctified over the Circle. Same can be said about a Tyranical Carthian State or a Ordo Dracul Magocracy. To further reiterate this point, think back to Requiem for Rome and see this first hand. In the time of the Camarilla the nascent Lancea et Sanctum was the ultimate underdog in the face of the ever present Legion of the Dead and Tyranical Senex. The Wing of Oracles had a monopoly on magical power so long as the gods looked favorably upon the Senex, and the College of Strangers was the only group willing to even consider aiding the budding Cult of Longinus, and even then they would have dropped them like a hat should a more profitable ally made themselves available. (Tangent: still to this day believe the College of Strangers is the true progenitor to the modern day Invictus.)<br /> <br /> The inescapable trapping of Christianity will effect one's opinions of the Covenant and how well they can sympathize with their twisted parasitic beliefs, but people can have either good or bad experiences with religion. Every one of us instinctively want's to root for who we think is the underdog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 10-12-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:58:37-08:00","id":1012298,"title":"","content":"Morality wise, I prefer the Lancea Sanctum over the Circle of the Crone for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum are ironically more tolerant than their mortal counterparts, they realize that for their sins they are damned to Hell but they spend their Requiems shepherding humanity to salvation, think about it, this isn't the biased politically-induced version of Christianity we all know and hate, this is the fundamental teachings of Jesus that built Christianity as a religion of love and tolerance, but more deadly.<br /> <br /> I mean while they would still be dicks and terrorize people for petty sins such as premarital sex or thievery, they would also target &quot;Christian&quot; hate-groups such as the KKK and homophobic gay bashers for not adhering to Jesus's message of love.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone on the other hand, are monsters, it's that simple.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm not Christian, and I never was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 12-04-2016, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T19:54:57-08:00","id":1012349,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I root for the Acolytes because their book was written better. It did an excellent job selling their way of unlife as sympathetic and desirable, while the Sanctum came off as a pack of hypocrites who praised Humanity with one breath and complained about being tied to it in the next.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the 2E writeup for the Sanctum seems to be pointing them away from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T20:45:44-08:00","id":1012362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1012349#post1012349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I root for the Acolytes because their book was written better. It did an excellent job selling their way of unlife as sympathetic and desirable, while the Sanctum came off as a pack of hypocrites who praised Humanity with one breath and complained about being tied to it in the next.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the 2E writeup for the Sanctum seems to be pointing them away from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.^<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T20:56:28-08:00","id":1012367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1012298#post1012298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morality wise, I prefer the Lancea Sanctum over the Circle of the Crone for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum are ironically more tolerant than their mortal counterparts, they realize that for their sins they are damned to Hell but they spend their Requiems shepherding humanity to salvation, think about it, this isn't the biased politically-induced version of Christianity we all know and hate, this is the fundamental teachings of Jesus that built Christianity as a religion of love and tolerance, but more deadly.<br /> <br /> I mean while they would still be dicks and terrorize people for petty sins such as premarital sex or thievery, they would also target &quot;Christian&quot; hate-groups such as the KKK and homophobic gay bashers for not adhering to Jesus's message of love.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone on the other hand, are monsters, it's that simple.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm not Christian, and I never was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean. They target the pure as much or more than the wicked. They're trying to reenact the story of Job. They find apparently righteous folk and test them. If they pass, sure. Or maybe they keep testing. If the target fails, they recruit. The write-up in 2e seems to focus very heavily on temptation as much or more than punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:43:30-08:00","id":1012409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1012367#post1012367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean. They target the pure as much or more than the wicked. They're trying to reenact the story of Job. They find apparently righteous folk and test them. If they pass, sure. Or maybe they keep testing. If the target fails, they recruit. The write-up in 2e seems to focus very heavily on temptation as much or more than punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also do something similar with a LS npc, but more of a way as justifying feeding off the supposed pure and righteous. The holiest fruit tastes the sweetest, but it would be sacrilegious to defame and pollute the fruit with the bite. So its like an extended method filtering the most 'almost' pure fruit to eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T07:02:25-08:00","id":1012557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1012367#post1012367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean. They target the pure as much or more than the wicked. They're trying to reenact the story of Job. They find apparently righteous folk and test them. If they pass, sure. Or maybe they keep testing. If the target fails, they recruit. The write-up in 2e seems to focus very heavily on temptation as much or more than punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>No wonder they have so many Daeva among their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:11:55-08:00","id":1012681,"title":"","content":"I probably missed it... <i>or</i> I'm just misremembering something, but wasn't there a character in Chicago who basically felt that the Circle's ideology was to stab people in the back because &quot;trials make you better&quot;? Can't recall at all how much that tied back into core Circle dogma, but there is that whole ultra-Darwinian (if not Randian) undercurrent.<br /> <br /> By way of contrast, the LeS/LS are (presented) as a Church, and part of their typical practice is helping new vampires transition &quot;into the night&quot;. Superficially/generically, the Church offers greater support network for the faithful. <br /> <br /> Granted, any particular instantiation of either covenant could likely turn those aspects around. Plus, the once-comforting support network might wind up forcing betrayal of scruples - and woe to the one who the group believes refused to properly give back. (etc., etc.)<br /> <br /> My 2 cents on the main topic? A lot of people who are attracted to this genre harbor negative views of Christianity - and either downplay or disbelieve the positive aspects. For various reasons (exposure via media scandals, resident hypocrites and/or not living in an area that really needs much 'help' from churches), it's easy to automatically assume that a Christian is a hypocrite - that the LeS/LS are just self-righteous whining jerks. In contrast, these biases are flipped for the Circle. The negatives are underplayed - possibly in part because the faiths which would be embraced/corrupted by the Circle don't have as much exposure in our culture - except as victims of Christian overreach. (Particularly in the US, with the whole freedom of religion thing that is constantly under siege...)<br /> <br /> &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; games insinuate that we should paint darker shadows around the games' institutions - and we have so many examples of hypocritical perversions of Christian principles (thanks to history, books and current events, etc.) that it is so easy to just paint the LeS/LS as irredeemable. But, I feel like that's a bit myopic - after all, the heroes of the CoC are Loki and Non-Sorbo-Hercules; but the mythic heroes of the LeS/LS can include Galahad and St. George. Personally, I feel like something is lost if one approaches a covenant as if all members were just hypocrites - as if there were only shadows, and no light. Because I think the thematic horror is made more meaningful when, instead, that light is embraced - and <i>then</i> twisted.<br /> <br /> Wow. That wasn't so much a run-on ramble as a train wreck of language. Sorry for the ... well, that. I'd fix it up, but must work. And/or sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:10:55-08:00","id":1014040,"title":"","content":"For me it comes down to a freedom vs restriction, both in character and in making characters.<br /> <br /> Crones are really a catch all covenant, which means you can get some really diverse and interesting characters and cruac styles coexisting. In my current game, we have a sect of very clinical, almost scientific cruac users and another sect who are more traditional wild and sacrificial cruac. Every individual has their own spin on it, very easy to get really cool themes going.<br /> <br /> Lancea on the otherhand is strict and unbending. There is room for some individualism, but it still feels constraining when designing a Lancea character.<br /> <br /> Not saying Lancea doesn't have its place, just that for PC's, not exactly the most tempting of choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11516-forgelineage","name":"ForgeLineage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:34:44-08:00","id":1015102,"title":"","content":"In practice, both Covenants are a bunch of murderous knobs who torment and kill people for their ideology, but one of them is at least not sanctimonious and self-righteous about it, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:24:40-08:00","id":1015139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1015102#post1015102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, both Covenants are a bunch of murderous knobs who torment and kill people for their ideology, but one of them is at least not sanctimonious and self-righteous about it, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more. There's nothing more insufferable than an animal skin clad vampire that believes their bloody religious practices are the one true way to bring enlightenment to all vampire, and has the gaul to torpor you and then have themselves and their pals ritualistically hunt you like it's the god damn bronze ages because you're in the wrong for criticizing their &quot;sacred practice&quot; of abandoning the 2nd Tradition. What a bunch of sanctimonious assholes...well, maybe not the only sanctimonious assholes though...shit! Ok, at least definitely we agree they're both murderous nobs who torment and kill people for their ideology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:42:35-08:00","id":1015144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1015139#post1015139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ritualistically hunt you like it's the god damn bronze ages because you're in the wrong for criticizing their &quot;sacred practice&quot; of abandoning the 2nd Tradition</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle in general doesn't abandon any tradition. But the second tradition is about siring another at peril to both yourself and your progeny, I don't think it's possible to really abandon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:54:15-08:00","id":1015147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1015144#post1015144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Circle in general doesn't abandon any tradition. But the second tradition is about siring another at peril to both yourself and your progeny, I don't think it's possible to really abandon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I'm 90% sure the 2nd Edition Core book's write up of the Circle specifically states that the 2nd Tradition practically doesn't exist in Crone dominated cities, in the &quot;When we are in power&quot; section.<br /> <br /> That being said...the main point of my last post is that self-righteousness and zealotry aren't universal for the Sanctified because the Chapel &amp; Spear and Mother's Army are religions at heart, and thus open to personal interpretation. By my own logic, the above statement is only true if you want your specific Circle domain to be that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":"Acknowledgement 12-09-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T21:01:52-08:00","id":1015148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1015147#post1015147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. I'm 90% sure the 2nd Edition Core book's write up of the Circle specifically states that the 2nd Tradition practically doesn't exist in Crone dominated cities, in the &quot;When we are in power&quot; section.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't mention the traditions at all in the Circle write up. You might be thinking of this, 'Less anarchy, and more the rule of the strong without formal laws or any pretense of &quot;civilization.&quot;'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> T<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">hat being said...the main point of my last post is that self-righteousness and zealotry aren't universal for the Sanctified because the Chapel &amp; Spear and Mother's Army are religions at heart, and thus open to personal interpretation. By my own logic, the above statement is only true if you want your specific Circle domain to be that way.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Lancea et Sanctum is a religion. The Circle of the Crone is a spiritual practice.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-10-2016, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T21:07:32-08:00","id":1015150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1015148#post1015148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't mention the traditions at all in the Circle write up. You might be thinking of this, 'Less anarchy, and more the rule of the strong without formal laws or any pretense of &amp;quot;civilization.&amp;quot;'</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? Not trying to second guess you either, I can't actually access my copy of 2nd Edition right now since I don't have a computer. I would have sworn that that exact line was in the Circle of the Crone section...or maybe in the section about the Traditions? I don't know anymore! T ^ T","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T21:28:32-08:00","id":1015154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=1015150#post1015150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure? Not trying to second guess you either, I can't actually access my copy of 2nd Edition right now since I don't have a computer. I would have sworn that that exact line was in the Circle of the Crone section...or maybe in the section about the Traditions? I don't know anymore! T ^ T</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked more, it just wasn't in the covenant section.<br /> <br /> P66, it's in the cities and domains section, specifically under the Theocracy. 'Spirituality is powerful leverage in politics. Look at the mortals. As secular as countries like the U.S. have become, they are still swayed by the clash of religions. A city is dominated by the Lancea et Sanctum. Midnight Mass is conducted before every Elysium. Attendance is not officially mandatory, but everyone knows what is good for her. The Traditions are held to the letter, punishments for infringement are severe. Alternatively, the Circle of the Crone runs the late night show. A grand hierophant oversees the domain through various priests and priestesses. Everyone has bled on the altar. Everyone has seen strange and terrible things that bind them together. The Second Tradition all but does not exist here.'<br /> <br /> And apparently the Second Tradition doesn't allow for Embraces, but is often used as a reason for whoever's in charge to limit them, or punish sires or childer for the mistakes of the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T21:39:04-08:00","id":1015155,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, thank you. That was really eating away at me because I knew I read that line somewhere in 2nd Edition. (Should have guessed it was the city building section, man 2nd Edition core is sooooo well written.) <br /> <br /> In light of that, you're entirely right. My logic has no ground to stand on since my quote was an example, and not a normative state. The Circle can have any take or opinion on the 2nd Tradition, as fits the story and the Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}